E["npc:brother-sarno"] = {t="npc",n="Brother Sarno",z="gnomeregan",s="Brother Sarno is an affable human cleric stationed at the entrance of the Cathedral of Light in Stormwind City. Serving as the primary greeter for worshipers and visitors, he also helps direct brave Alliance travelers toward engineers in Ironforge who need aid in reclaiming Gnomeregan.",h="Brother Sarno is an affable human cleric stationed at the entrance of the Cathedral of Light in Stormwind...",sec={{t="A Welcoming Voice in the Cathedral",b="Standing just inside the archways of Stormwind's magnificent Cathedral of Light, Brother Sarno is often the very first face pilgrims and travelers encounter. As a dedicated brother of the Church of the Holy Light, his role is simple yet vital: offering a kind greeting to anyone who enters the sacred hall seeking solace, prayer, or guidance. His warmth extends even to the most unexpected visitors, making him a reassuring presence amid the city's busy clerical life.",sp=0},{t="Ties to Ironforge",b="Beyond his pastoral greetings, Brother Sarno maintains communication with allies across the Alliance. When Tinkmaster Overspark in Ironforge urgently needed assistance dealing with his rogue invention, Techbot, deep within the irradiated halls of Gnomeregan, Sarno took it upon himself to guide capable adventurers toward Dun Morogh. Though a humble brother of the cloth, he understands that supporting the displaced gnomes is an act of genuine fraternity.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where can I find Brother Sarno?",a="Brother Sarno is located inside the Cathedral of Light in Stormwind City's Cathedral Square. He stands just to the left of the main entrance, ready to greet anyone who walks through the doors.",al={"sarno location","where is brother sarno","cathedral greeter"}},{q="What does Brother Sarno do?",a="Sarno serves as a welcoming attendant for the Church of the Holy Light, greeting visitors and worshipers. He also directs adventurers to Tinkmaster Overspark in Ironforge to assist with troubles brewing in Gnomeregan.",al={"brother sarno role","what does sarno do"}},{q="Why does a Stormwind priest send people to Gnomeregan?",a="The Church of the Holy Light promotes cooperation and aid across the Grand Alliance. When word reached the clergy that Tinkmaster Overspark needed help reclaiming errant technology like Techbot, Brother Sarno helped steer capable champions toward Ironforge to assist.",al={"sarno gnomeregan quest","why does sarno care about gnomes"}},{q="Does he belong to any specific order?",a="He is an ordained member of the Church of the Holy Light, serving beneath the leadership of the cathedral's prelates and Archbishop Benedictus in Stormwind.",al={"sarno faction","brother sarno order"}}},ang={["class:Priest"]="Brother Sarno is the welcoming hand of your order in Stormwind, modeling the hospitality and gentle grace central to the virtues of the Holy Light.",["race:Gnome"]="Despite serving in a human house of worship, Brother Sarno gladly steers willing hands toward Ironforge to support Gnomeregan's recovery efforts."},kw={"brother sarno","cathedral of light","church of the holy light","stormwind","techbot","tinkmaster overspark"},rel={"subzone:cathedral-of-light","quest:2923","zone:stormwind","topic:church-of-the-holy-light","zone:ironforge","zone:gnomeregan","topic:light"},src={"Brother Sarno"}}
E["npc:dark-iron-ambassador"] = {t="npc",n="Dark Iron Ambassador",z="gnomeregan",s="Deep within the irradiated halls of Gnomeregan lurks the Dark Iron Ambassador, an elusive emissary sent by Emperor Dagran Thaurissan. His presence reveals that the fall of the gnome capital involves far more than just wild trogg incursions and madness.",h="Deep within the irradiated halls of Gnomeregan lurks the Dark Iron Ambassador, an elusive emissary sent by...",sec={{t="A Shadowy Envoy",b="While Gnomeregan's catastrophic downfall is publicly blamed on the trogg invasion and High Tinker Mekkatorque's desperate radiation gambit, the presence of the Dark Iron Ambassador points to far darker machinations. Wandering the contaminated depths of the workshop corridors, this rare Dark Iron dwarf suggests that Sicco Thermaplugg did not betray his people in complete isolation.",sp=0},{t="Conspiracies in the Deep",b="The true motives behind Emperor Thaurissan's envoy remain cloaked in secrecy and speculation. Both Alliance investigators in Ironforge and Horde-affiliated goblins have raised theories about the Dark Iron clan's involvement in the subterranean disaster. Rumors swirl that the Dark Irons offered technical expertise, aided Thermaplugg in operating heavy machinery like the subterranean super rig, or brokered a vile pact to undercut Ironforge from below.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is the Dark Iron Ambassador?",a="He is an envoy of the Dark Iron clan found deep inside the irradiated ruin of Gnomeregan. His role is that of a diplomatic representative between Emperor Dagran Thaurissan and the rogue forces controlling the fallen city.",al={"who is this dwarf","dark iron ambassador identity","what is dark iron ambassador"}},{q="Why is a Dark Iron dwarf inside Gnomeregan?",a="His presence strongly suggests secret negotiations between the Dark Iron clan and the mad usurper Sicco Thermaplugg. The Dark Irons appear to have had a hand in assisting Thermaplugg or exploiting Gnomeregan's disaster for their own ends against Ironforge.",al={"why are dark irons in gnomeregan","what is he doing here","dark iron dwarf purpose"}},{q="Did the Dark Irons help cause the fall of Gnomeregan?",a="While the trogg invasion itself drove the initial crisis, in-universe conspiracies and goblin observers suggest the Dark Irons secretly assisted Thermaplugg. They may have aided in drilling operations or provided technical help with advanced subterranean equipment.",al={"did dark irons cause trogg invasion","dark iron conspiracy","did thaurissan help thermaplugg"}},{q="Where does the ambassador come from?",a="He represents the Dark Iron clan, ruled by Emperor Dagran Thaurissan from their stronghold beneath the Blackrock Mountain. He was dispatched to treat with Gnomeregan's traitorous new leadership.",al={"where is ambassador from","who sent him","who does he work for"}},{q="Is he allied with Sicco Thermaplugg?",a="Yes, evidence strongly points to an alliance. As an envoy, his survival among Thermaplugg's leper gnomes and mechanostriders demonstrates an ongoing diplomatic link rather than hostility between the two factions.",al={"thermaplugg dark iron ally","is he with thermaplugg","working with thermaplugg"}},{q="Where can the Dark Iron Ambassador be found?",a="He is an elusive, rare encounter who wanders the contaminated engineering sectors and workshop corridors inside the Gnomeregan dungeon.",al={"ambassador spawn location","where does he spawn","ambassador gnomeregan location"}}},ang={["race:Gnome"]="Finding a Dark Iron envoy in Gnomeregan proves the horrific betrayal that poisoned your home was backed by dwarf enemies from Blackrock.",["race:Dwarf"]="Your ancient Dark Iron kin have wormed their way into the gnome halls, demonstrating that Thaurissan's reach threatens Khaz Modan from within.",["faction:Alliance"]="The ambassador's secret dealings with Thermaplugg represent an active hostile front right on the doorstep of Ironforge."},kw={"conspiracy","dark iron ambassador","dark iron clan","gnomeregan","super rig","thaurissan","thermaplugg"},rel={"npc:sicco-thermaplugg","zone:gnomeregan","topic:dark-iron-clan","topic:dark-iron-dwarf","quest:2947","quest:2904","zone:ironforge","topic:gnome"},src={"Dark Iron Ambassador"}}
E["npc:electrocutioner-6000"] = {t="npc",n="Electrocutioner 6000",z="gnomeregan",s="The Electrocutioner 6000 is a deadly, super-charged spider tank deployed to defend the Launch Bay within the irradiated halls of Gnomeregan. Piloted by the notorious leper gnome Lieutenant Tom 'Sizzlepants' Crankle, it represents Mekgineer Thermaplugg's reckless ambition to weaponize high-voltage electricity.",h="The Electrocutioner 6000 is a deadly, super-charged spider tank deployed to defend the Launch Bay within the...",sec={{t="Thermaplugg's Shocking Prototype",b="Mekgineer Thermaplugg has never been known for rigorous safety testing. Driven by megalomania and haste, he regularly rushes unproven war machines straight from the drawing board into live combat. The Electrocutioner 6000 was his initial attempt to harness raw electrical currents as an offensive system mounted to an armored spider tank chassis. Rather than working out lethal power surges in a laboratory, Thermaplugg sent it immediately to guard the upper tiers of Gnomeregan's Launch Bay.",sp=0},{t="Lieutenant 'Sizzlepants'",b="Operating experimental machinery is often a death sentence, particularly when lethal voltage is involved. Early test pilots perished in agonizing mishaps, but Lieutenant Tom Crankle managed to withstand the lethal surges and survived at the controls. Earning the grim moniker 'Sizzlepants,' he became an idol of resilience among the irradiated leper gnomes loyal to Thermaplugg, fiercely guarding the path toward the inner workshops.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where can the Electrocutioner 6000 be found?",a="The Electrocutioner 6000 is positioned on an elevated catwalk platform overlooking the Launch Bay inside the fallen city of Gnomeregan.",al={"electrocutioner 6000 location","where is electrocutioner","find electrocutioner 6000"}},{q="Who pilots the Electrocutioner 6000?",a="It is piloted by Lieutenant Tom Crankle, better known as 'Sizzlepants.' He is a crazed leper gnome officer who achieved renown among Thermaplugg's forces as the sole pilot to survive the tank's dangerous internal electrical discharge.",al={"who drives electrocutioner 6000","sizzlepants","tom sizzlepants crankle","pilot of electrocutioner"}},{q="Why is the machine so volatile?",a="Mekgineer Thermaplugg refuses to spend time conducting proper safety evaluations, preferring to rush inventions immediately into service. The Electrocutioner 6000 was his first trial with an electrified spider tank, leaving its lethal power feeds volatile and perilous even to its own operator.",al={"why does it shock","electrocutioner prototype","thermaplugg design"}},{q="Why is defeating the Electrocutioner 6000 important for explorers?",a="The pilot holds the Workshop Key, an essential device that unlocks the back door entrance into Gnomeregan's deeper engineering sectors, allowing strike teams a faster route through the reclaimed facilities.",al={"workshop key","why kill electrocutioner","electrocutioner 6000 loot"}},{q="What happens to the machine after it is destroyed?",a="Following its defeat, Alliance scavengers and tinkerers have retrieved components of the ruined chassis—including the celebrated Electrocutioner Leg—and brought them back to Tinker Town in Ironforge for study and safekeeping.",al={"electrocutioner leg","salvage electrocutioner","ironforge trophy"}},{q="Is the Electrocutioner an automaton or a vehicle?",a="It is a modified spider tank, functioning as an armored mechano-vehicle guided manually by its pilot from an internal cockpit, rather than an autonomous robotic construct.",al={"is electrocutioner a robot","electrocutioner spider tank type"}}},ang={["race:Gnome"]="For the exiled gnomes of Ironforge, the Electrocutioner 6000 is an insult to their craft: a dangerous, untested monstrosity that reflects Thermaplugg's twisted disregard for proper engineering ethics and gnome lives.",["profession:Engineering"]="Engineers marvel at the raw high-voltage output harnessed within the chassis, even if Thermaplugg's reckless lack of grounding makes it a lethal hazard to its own crew.",["faction:Alliance"]="Breaching the Launch Bay and eliminating Crankle is vital to securing the Workshop Key, bypassing hazardous front corridors during liberation efforts into Gnomeregan."},kw={"crankle","electrocutioner","gnomeregan","launch bay","sizzlepants","spider tank","thermaplugg","workshop key"},rel={"zone:gnomeregan","subzone:launch-bay","topic:leper-gnome","subzone:tinker-town","topic:gnome","zone:ironforge"},src={"Electrocutioner 6000"}}
E["npc:kernobee"] = {t="npc",n="Kernobee",z="gnomeregan",s="Kernobee is a goblin engineer trapped deep within the ruined halls of Gnomeregan. After stumbling upon dangerous secrets involving Dark Iron dwarf sabotage, he was captured, beaten unconscious, and left to die among the troggs in the dormitory quarters.",h="Kernobee is a goblin engineer trapped deep within the ruined halls of Gnomeregan.",sec={{t="A Deadly Discovery",b="While conducting business or scavenging within the fallen gnome capital, Kernobee uncovered a grave secret: the Dark Iron dwarves were directly involved in the construction and operation of the massive super rig burrowing beneath the city. Realizing the immense value—and lethality—of this intelligence, he attempted to flee immediately to Ratchet to deliver word to his associate, Tinkerwiz. Unfortunately, the Dark Irons caught him before he could make his escape.",sp=0},{t="Left for the Troggs",b="Rather than killing him outright, his captors battered Kernobee unconscious and tossed him into a small room along the dormitory corridor, opposite the Clean Zone. Left stranded among feral troggs and radiation fallout, the battered goblin depends entirely on passing adventurers to revive him and shield him until he can reach safety.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Kernobee?",a="Kernobee is a goblin operative found unconscious inside Gnomeregan's dormitory sector. He works closely with Tinkerwiz in Ratchet and ventured into the ruins before being ambushed.",al={"who is this goblin","kernobee lore","about kernobee"}},{q="Why was Kernobee imprisoned in Gnomeregan?",a="Kernobee discovered that the Dark Iron clan was covertly helping construct the subterranean super rig machines inside the city. To keep their presence and sabotage quiet, the Dark Irons incapacitated him and threw him into the dormitory to perish.",al={"why is he here","why did dark irons capture him","why in dormitory"}},{q="Who does Kernobee report to?",a="He reports to Tinkerwiz, a goblin engineer stationed across the sea in the neutral port town of Ratchet in the Barrens.",al={"who is tinkerwiz","where is he going","ratchet connection"}},{q="Where in Gnomeregan is Kernobee located?",a="He is slumped unconscious in a small side room on the lower level of the Dormitory, situated on the western side directly across from the Clean Zone.",al={"kernobee location","where is kernobee","find kernobee"}}},ang={["race:Gnome"]="For gnomes fighting to reclaim their homeland, Kernobee's intelligence is alarming proof that their catastrophe was aided from the shadows by Dark Iron dwarven meddling.",["profession:Engineering"]="Engineers can appreciate the sheer hazard of poking around experimental subterranean machinery like the Dark Iron rigs when rival schematics are at stake."},kw={"dark iron","dormitory","gnomeregan","kernobee","ratchet","super rig","tinkerwiz"},rel={"quest:2904","zone:gnomeregan","subzone:dormitory","subzone:clean-zone","subzone:ratchet","topic:goblin","topic:trogg","topic:gnome"},src={"Kernobee"}}
E["npc:nogg"] = {t="npc",n="Nogg",z="gnomeregan",s="Nogg is a goblin engineer operating out of Nogg's Machine Shop in the Drag of Orgrimmar. He offers tinkering expertise and specialized craftsmanship to the Horde, notably analyzing strange mechanical salvage recovered from deep within Gnomeregan.",h="Nogg is a goblin engineer operating out of Nogg's Machine Shop in the Drag of Orgrimmar.",sec={{t="Nogg's Machine Shop",b="Tucked away in the shaded corridors of the Drag in Orgrimmar, Nogg runs an independent engineering workshop catering to adventurers and craftsmen alike. While the surrounding city relies heavily on traditional orcish steel and brute strength, Nogg provides the specialized mechanical finesse that only a goblin can offer. He maintains a keen interest in foreign contraptions and tech, happily examining curious trinkets and mechanical oddities dragged back from Alliance lands or subterranean ruins.",sp=0},{t="Gnomish Gadgets and Salvage",b="Nogg takes special interest in items recovered from the fallen gnomish capital of Gnomeregan. When Horde operatives retrieve intricate rings or technological remnants from the irradiated vaults across the sea, Nogg is one of the few minds in Durotar capable of disassembling, deciphering, and retrofitting such bizarre clockwork mechanisms for Horde use.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where can I find Nogg?",a="Nogg is located in the Drag inside Orgrimmar, running his own workshop known as Nogg's Machine Shop.",al={"nogg location","where is nogg","nogg's machine shop"}},{q="What is Nogg's connection to Gnomeregan?",a="When Horde adventurers venture into the irradiated tunnels of Gnomeregan in Khaz Modan, they can salvage intricate technological trinkets. Nogg is the local expert in Orgrimmar who inspects and reconfigures these foreign gnomish rings.",al={"why nogg gnomeregan","nogg ring","return of the ring"}},{q="Is Nogg part of the Horde?",a="Nogg is an independent goblin artisan operating directly within Orgrimmar, actively serving Horde adventurers and lending his technical skills to their war effort.",al={"is nogg horde","nogg faction"}},{q="Can Nogg alter or reforge rings?",a="Yes. If an adventurer brings him a Sparklematic-extracted ring from Gnomeregan and desires different enchantments or mechanical properties, Nogg knows how to dismantle and rebuild the piece to better suit their needs.",al={"ring redo","change gnomeregan ring"}}},ang={["profession:Engineering"]="Fellow engineers often stop by Nogg's Machine Shop in the Drag to pick up parts, talk shop, and marvel at how easily goblin hands repurpose intricate gnomish tech.",["faction:Horde"]="For Horde warriors returning from dangerous operations in the Eastern Kingdoms, Nogg bridges the gap between crude salvage and finely calibrated battle gear."},kw={"gnomeregan","goblin engineer","machine shop","nogg","orgrimmar","return of the ring","the drag"},rel={"subzone:drag","zone:orgrimmar","quest:2947","quest:2950","zone:gnomeregan","topic:goblin","topic:horde"},src={"Nogg"}}
E["npc:ozzie-togglevolt"] = {t="npc",n="Ozzie Togglevolt",z="gnomeregan",s="Ozzie Togglevolt is a gnome engineer and survivor of Gnomeregan's fall, currently operating out of the snowy village of Kharanos in Dun Morogh. Haunted by the tragedy that struck his people, he works alongside his partner Razzle Sprysprocket to research a remedy for the irradiated leper gnomes.",h="Ozzie Togglevolt is a gnome engineer and survivor of Gnomeregan's fall, currently operating out of the snowy...",sec={{t="Escape from the Deep",b="Ozzie Togglevolt was inside the subterranean wonders of Gnomeregan when catastrophe struck. When the toxic fallout was vented throughout the corridors to stem the trogg invasion, Ozzie stood right beside his fellow gnome, Gnoarn. A sudden radioactive discharge struck Gnoarn directly, altering him forever before Ozzie's eyes. Though Ozzie made it to the surface alive and reached the haven of Dun Morogh, the horrifying memory of that disaster never left him.",sp=0},{t="The Kharanos Workshop",b="Now established in Kharanos, Ozzie spends his days tinkering alongside Razzle Sprysprocket. Despite minor mishaps and defensive scrambles against encroaching Frostmane trolls, their primary technological and scientific endeavor remains intensely personal: finding a way to reverse the horrific mutagenic fallout of their lost home and cure the suffering leper gnomes.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Ozzie Togglevolt?",a="Ozzie Togglevolt is a gnomish engineer residing in Kharanos in Dun Morogh. He fled the radioactive devastation of Gnomeregan and now dedicates his technical expertise toward finding a cure for his afflicted brethren.",al={"who is ozzie","ozzie togglevolt lore","kharanos gnome ozzie"}},{q="What is Ozzie trying to cure?",a="Ozzie and his colleague Razzle Sprysprocket are researching a method to cleanse the toxic irradiation that turned so many of their kin into madness-stricken leper gnomes.",al={"what is ozzie researching","ozzie leper gnome cure","cure for leper gnomes"}},{q="Who is Gnoarn to Ozzie?",a="Gnoarn was with Ozzie in Gnomeregan when the toxic vents were unleashed. Ozzie witnessed a radioactive bolt strike Gnoarn directly, a tragic incident that drove Ozzie's obsession with reversing the contamination.",al={"ozzie and gnoarn","what happened to gnoarn","who is gnoarn"}},{q="Who is working with Ozzie in Kharanos?",a="Ozzie works alongside Razzle Sprysprocket. Together, they tinker in Kharanos, developing concoctions and gathering contaminated field specimens to analyze the radioactive fallout.",al={"ozzie partner","who is razzle","razzle sprysprocket"}},{q="Did Ozzie help defend Kharanos from trolls?",a="Yes. When a massive Frostmane troll assaulted Kharanos, Ozzie and Razzle attempted to fend it off by hurling what they thought were impact grenades, only to discover they were actually delayed time bombs before fellow inventor Lazlo Grindwidget intervened.",al={"ozzie troll attack","frostmane troll kharanos","ozzie grenades"}},{q="What quests does Ozzie offer?",a="Ozzie enlists travelers in Dun Morogh to gather irradiated residues and components from around Gnomeregan through tasks such as 'The Day After', 'Gnogaine', and 'The Only Cure is More Green Glow'.",al={"ozzie quests","togglevolt quests","what quests does ozzie give"}}},ang={["race:Gnome"]="For gnome adventurers, Ozzie represents the grief and determination of the survivors of Gnomeregan, refusing to abandon irradiated kin to their fate.",["profession:Engineering"]="Ozzie showcases the trial-and-error realities of gnome craftsmanship, where devices can backfire dramatically in combat or yield ingenious breakthroughs in biochemical decontamination.",["faction:Alliance"]="Stationed right outside Ironforge in Kharanos, Ozzie aids travelers while maintaining Alliance footholds in the frigid hills of Dun Morogh."},kw={"dun morogh","gnoarn","gnomeregan","kharanos","leper gnome","ozzie","radiation","razzle","sprysprocket","togglevolt"},rel={"npc:razzle-sprysprocket","npc:gnoarn","topic:leper-gnome","subzone:kharanos","zone:gnomeregan","quest:2927","quest:2926","quest:2962"},src={"Ozzie Togglevolt"}}
E["npc:scooty"] = {t="npc",n="Scooty",z="gnomeregan",s="Scooty is a goblin engineer operating out of the bustling pirate port of Booty Bay. Proclaiming himself a master of engineering, he maintains a delicate transponder setup linked directly to an experimental teleporter in the fallen city of Gnomeregan. His contraptions offer Horde operatives a direct, if perilous, technological bypass right into the heart of Dun Morogh.",h="Scooty is a goblin engineer operating out of the bustling pirate port of Booty Bay.",sec={{t="Booty Bay's Teleportation Expert",b="Operating amid the wharves and workshops of Booty Bay, Scooty holds court as one of the Steamwheedle Cartel's most ambitious tinkerers. While typical goblins obsess over gunpowder and explosives, Scooty turned his attention to instantaneous molecular transport. By calibrating complex transponder systems, he manages a direct operational link to a teleportation pad situated inside Gnomeregan. Horde forces looking to breach the subterranean gnome stronghold rely heavily on Scooty's tinkering to bypass treacherous Alliance territory altogether.",sp=0},{t="Gnomish Gadgets and Goblin Risk",b="Maintaining experimental goblin teleporters is rarely a dull enterprise. Between faulty transponder coils and the chaotic fallout inside irradiated Gnomeregan, Scooty regularly enlists adventurers to retrieve lost data, test field components, and fix disastrous technical malfunctions. Despite the obvious physical perils involved in being dematerialized across continents, Scooty remains entirely confident in his genius, dismissing every catastrophic mechanical hiccup as merely a minor obstacle on the road to true innovation.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Scooty?",a="Scooty is a goblin engineer based in Booty Bay who claims the title of master engineer. He maintains and calibrates the Goblin Transponder network that connects Southern Stranglethorn directly to an experimental teleporter pad deep inside Gnomeregan.",al={"who is scooty","scooty lore","scooty npc","booty bay scooty"}},{q="Why does Scooty have a teleporter to Gnomeregan?",a="Scooty established a link with an experimental teleportation pad inside Gnomeregan to facilitate direct travel into the gnome city. For the Horde, his device provides a vital back door into Dun Morogh without needing to fight across heavily fortified Alliance homelands.",al={"why gnomeregan teleporter","how does scooty teleporter work","scooty port to gnomer"}},{q="Where is Scooty located?",a="Scooty can be found working in Booty Bay, the neutral goblin port city located at the southern tip of Stranglethorn Vale.",al={"where is scooty","scooty location","find scooty"}},{q="Is using Scooty's teleporter safe?",a="Goblin engineering is infamous for unpredictable malfunctions, and Scooty's teleporter is no exception. While it successfully sends adventurers into Gnomeregan, mechanical mishaps and miscalibrated transponders are a constant hazard when trusting his volatile technology.",al={"is scooty safe","teleporter safe","teleporter risks"}}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="Scooty provides the Horde with an indispensable shortcut into Gnomeregan, letting your strike teams bypass ironclad Alliance defenses in Dun Morogh.",["profession:Engineering"]="Fellow tinkerers will appreciate Scooty's audacious application of transponder physics, even if typical goblin disregard for basic safety protocols makes every activation a gamble."},kw={"booty bay","gnomeregan","goblin","scooty","stranglethorn","teleporter","transponder"},rel={"subzone:booty-bay","zone:gnomeregan","quest:2904","topic:goblin","topic:gnome"},src={"Scooty"}}
E["npc:sicco-thermaplugg"] = {t="npc",n="Sicco Thermaplugg",z="gnomeregan",s="Mekgineer Sicco Thermaplugg is the self-proclaimed ruler of ruined Gnomeregan and the greatest traitor in gnomish history. Once the chief advisor and closest friend of High Tinker Gelbin Mekkatorque, he orchestrated the catastrophic irradiation of the underground city in a twisted bid to seize power. Now thoroughly deranged and transformed into a leper gnome, he commands the irradiated halls from within a walking mechanostrider fortress.",h="Mekgineer Sicco Thermaplugg is the self-proclaimed ruler of ruined Gnomeregan and the greatest traitor in...",sec={{t="A Toxic Ambition",b="Sicco Thermaplugg studied alongside Gelbin Mekkatorque at Gearshaft University, and the two worked together on many early mechanical triumphs, including early siege engines. Gelbin considered him a brilliant friend, but Sicco festered with bitter envy, convinced his own labor was overshadowed by Gelbin's intuitive genius. When Mekkatorque was elected High Tinker, Sicco's resentment curdled into outright malice. Believing he alone possessed the ruthless vision needed to turn gnomish technology into geopolitical power, Sicco bided his time in the Tinkers' Court, looking for any opportunity to discredit his rival.",sp=0},{t="The Poisoning of Gnomeregan",b="When subterranean troggs swarmed Gnomeregan during the Third War, the gnomes fought alone in subterranean darkness for five desperate years. Seeking a way to break the siege without burdening the Alliance, Gelbin turned to Thermaplugg for counsel. Sicco presented fabricated schematics for a dense radioactive gas, claiming it would settle harmlessly in the lower tunnels and annihilate the troggs while gnomish life-support scrubbers protected the civilians above. In truth, Thermaplugg intentionally miscalculated the gas's volume and toxicity. He intended to inflict just enough casualties to unseat Mekkatorque from power and assume command himself.",sp=1},{t="King of the Ruins",b="Thermaplugg's calculations proved catastrophically wrong. The radioactive fallout swept uncontrollably through all levels of the city, slaughtering eighty percent of the gnomish population and twisting the survivors into feral, diseased leper gnomes. Instead of ascending the throne of a thriving metropolis, Sicco himself was warped by the fallout. Driven utterly mad by the radiation, he crowned himself King of the Gnomes and now presides over a charnel house of irradiated machines and mutated thralls, fighting a perpetual war against trogg invaders and any surface gnomes seeking to reclaim their lost home.",sp=2}},faq={{q="Who is Sicco Thermaplugg?",a="He is the former chief advisor to High Tinker Gelbin Mekkatorque who betrayed his people during the trogg invasion. Intending to usurp power, he convinced Mekkatorque to release radioactive gas into Gnomeregan, which resulted in the near-extinction of their race and left him ruling the irradiated ruins as a mad king.",al={"who is thermaplugg","thermaplugg lore","who is the boss in gnomeregan","thermaplugg backstory"}},{q="Why did Thermaplugg betray Gelbin Mekkatorque?",a="Thermaplugg suffered from intense jealousy toward Mekkatorque. He believed Gelbin was an overrated tinker whose election as High Tinker was unearned. Sicco also despised Gelbin's policy of sharing inventions freely with the Alliance, believing gnomish technology should instead be weaponized to forge a powerful, feared gnomish empire under his own leadership.",al={"why did he betray gnomeregan","thermaplugg motive","why does sicco hate gelbin"}},{q="Did Thermaplugg cause the trogg invasion?",a="The troggs originally broke through into Gnomeregan's lower levels after being unearthed from the ancient titan vault of Uldaman. While rumors swirl that Thermaplugg had prior knowledge of the subterranean breach or even facilitated it to engineer a crisis, Mekkatorque has never been able to verify whether Sicco initiated the invasion or simply exploited it.",al={"did he summon troggs","did sicco bring the troggs","trogg invasion gnomeregan origin"}},{q="What happened to Thermaplugg after the gas was released?",a="Like thousands of other gnomes caught in the disaster, Thermaplugg was exposed to lethal levels of radiation. The fallout withered his flesh, turned his skin a sickly green, and fractured his mind. Instead of fleeing with the surviving refugees to Ironforge, he stayed behind to rule the ruins as the self-proclaimed King of the Gnomes.",al={"is thermaplugg a leper gnome","how did he become a leper gnome","why is thermaplugg green"}},{q="What is the Crowd Pummeler 9-60?",a="The Crowd Pummeler 9-60 is a colossal security mech originally invented by Oglethorpe Obnoticus. Thermaplugg stole Obnoticus's blueprints, built a giant prototype, and unleashed it in the city. Sicco framed Obnoticus for the rampage, resulting in the inventor's exile while Thermaplugg kept the automaton as his personal guardian inside Gnomeregan.",al={"crowd pummeler origin","who made crowd pummeler","thermaplugg stolen inventions"}},{q="What does High Tinker Mekkatorque want done with Thermaplugg?",a="Mekkatorque considers Thermaplugg his greatest failure and his people's greatest traitor. From his temporary court in Ironforge's Tinker Town, Mekkatorque actively commissions brave Alliance adventurers to delve into the irradiated depths of Gnomeregan and execute Sicco to bring justice to the fallen.",al={"gelbin quest thermaplugg","kill thermaplugg quest","does mekkatorque want him dead"}}},ang={["race:Gnome"]="Thermaplugg is the embodiment of everything your people mourn and despise; his vanity and treachery cost you your homeland and turned your kin into diseased horrors.",["faction:Alliance"]="Thermaplugg's betrayal kept Gnomeregan from answering the call to arms in the Third War, crippling Alliance supply lines and engineering support during humanity's darkest hour.",["profession:Engineering"]="Thermaplugg represents the lethal hazard of sloppy formulas and unprincipled design, wielding hazardous walking war machines and toxic bomb Dispensers against anyone who enters his workshop.",["race:Dwarf"]="Your kin in Ironforge gave refuge to the ragged survivors fleeing Thermaplugg's poison, and Ironforge guards watch the Dun Morogh gates closely against his irradiated wanderers."},kw={"crowd pummeler","gnomeregan","leper gnome","mekkatorque","sicco","thermaplugg","tinkers court","trogg"},rel={"npc:gelbin-mekkatorque","zone:gnomeregan","topic:leper-gnome","topic:gnome","subzone:tinkers-court","zone:ironforge","topic:trogg","subzone:uldaman"},src={"Sicco Thermaplugg"}}
E["npc:talvash-del-kissel"] = {t="npc",n="Talvash del Kissel",z="gnomeregan",s="Talvash del Kissel is a down-on-his-luck gnome jeweler who fled the fall of Gnomeregan and now resides in Ironforge's Mystic Ward. Plagued by debt and persistent rumors following the loss of his home, he seeks capable adventurers to help recover lost treasures and restore shattered relics. His keen eye for precious gems and ancient baubles makes him a valuable contact for those plumbing the depths of Uldaman.",h="Talvash del Kissel is a down-on-his-luck gnome jeweler who fled the fall of Gnomeregan and now resides in...",sec={{t="From Artisan to Exiled Debtor",b="Once a respected jeweler in the technological heart of Gnomeregan, Talvash saw his livelihood obliterated alongside his home when the troggs overran the underground city. Escaping with the surviving refugees to the dwarven capital of Ironforge, he set up camp in the Mystic Ward. Unfortunately, relocation did not treat him kindly. Rumors of questionable dealings and unpaid obligations quickly piled up, sinking the craftsman into deep financial distress. Unable to rebuild his trade through conventional means, Talvash relies on freelance adventurers to retrieve lost assets and salvage his ruined reputation.",sp=0},{t="Relics of Uldaman and Gnomish Craft",b="Despite his misfortunes, Talvash has lost none of his gem-cutting precision or appraisal acumen. When explorers in the Badlands uncover an ancient, shattered necklace deep within the Titan vault of Uldaman, Talvash proves to be one of the few craftsmen in the Eastern Kingdoms capable of understanding its intricate enchantments. Restoring such power requires rare components and painstaking labor, but Talvash is eager to ply his trade—both to clear his debts and to prove his enduring skill.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Talvash del Kissel?",a="Talvash is an exiled gnome jeweler living in the Mystic Ward of Ironforge. Displaced after the fall of Gnomeregan, he now struggles with crushing debt and lingering rumors, hiring adventurers to help repair artifacts and settle his accounts.",al={"who is talvash","talvash del kissel","talvash"}},{q="Where can I find Talvash?",a="Talvash is located in the Mystic Ward of Ironforge, standing near the pond and magic-oriented shops in the dwarven capital.",al={"talvash location","where is talvash","find talvash del kissel"}},{q="What happened to his business in Gnomeregan?",a="Talvash ran a jewelry trade in Gnomeregan prior to its downfall. When troggs invaded and the city fell, he lost everything, and subsequent rumors and sour fortunes left him deeply indebted in Ironforge.",al={"why is talvash broke","talvash debt","what happened to talvash"}},{q="What is Talvash's connection to Uldaman?",a="Explorers who find a shattered power source within the ancient dig site of Uldaman are directed to Talvash. His expertise in gems and enchanting allows him to reconstruct the shattered necklace for adventurers capable of gathering the missing pieces.",al={"talvash uldaman","uldaman necklace","shattered necklace quest"}},{q="Does Talvash have anything to do with Gnomeregan quests?",a="Yes. He is involved in recovering lost personal items from the ruined city, including lost rings and devices left behind during the evacuation of Gnomeregan.",al={"talvash gnomeregan","return of the ring quest"}},{q="What is the origin of his name?",a="Talvash del Kissel was the character name of a gnome mage played by Shawn Carnes, a Blizzard quest lead, during his days playing EverQuest before working on World of Warcraft.",al={"talvash trivia","talvash name origin","shawn carnes"}}},ang={["race:Gnome"]="Talvash is a stark reminder of how the loss of Gnomeregan shattered ordinary civilian lives, reducing master craftsmen to broke exiles scraping by in Ironforge.",["faction:Alliance"]="Alliance adventurers delving into Uldaman or the ruins of Gnomeregan will find Talvash an essential contact for restoring ancient jewelry and recovering lost gnomish heirlooms."},kw={"del kissel","gnomeregan","ironforge","jeweler","mystic ward","shattered necklace","talvash","uldaman"},rel={"zone:ironforge","subzone:mystic-ward","zone:gnomeregan","subzone:uldaman","quest:2947","quest:2948","quest:8355","npc:shawn"},src={"Talvash del Kissel"}}
E["npc:viscous-fallout"] = {t="npc",n="Viscous Fallout",z="gnomeregan",s="Viscous Fallout is a corrupted water elemental wandering the irradiated corridors of Gnomeregan. Once a pure spirit inhabiting the city's pristine aquifers, it was twisted into a toxic monstrosity by Mekgineer Thermaplugg's devastating radiation release.",h="Viscous Fallout is a corrupted water elemental wandering the irradiated corridors of Gnomeregan.",sec={{t="A Polluted Spirit",b="Before the fall of Gnomeregan, the gnomish capital relied on sophisticated, intricate waterways and clean subterranean aquifers to power and sustain its mechanical marvels. A solitary water elemental dwelt peacefully within this pristine water supply. When Mekgineer Thermaplugg opened the radiation vents to wipe out the invading troggs, the resulting chemical contamination seeped deep into the city's reservoirs, trapping the elemental and corrupting its very substance.",sp=0},{t="Agony in the Runoff",b="Now, the creature is little more than a living pool of toxic sludge, drifting aimlessly through the irradiated lower passages. Transformed into an embodiment of Thermaplugg's treachery, Viscous Fallout lashes out at anything in its path, consumed by constant pain and fury. Striking it down is a grim necessity for those venturing into Gnomeregan to cleanse the tainted depths.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Viscous Fallout?",a="Viscous Fallout is a water elemental mini-boss located inside the ruined city of Gnomeregan. Formerly a pure water spirit native to the city's deep aquifers, it became thoroughly tainted by toxic sludge and radioactive fallout.",al={"who is viscous fallout","viscous fallout lore","what kind of mob is viscous fallout"}},{q="How did it become corrupted?",a="When Mekgineer Thermaplugg deliberately flooded Gnomeregan with radioactive waste to repel the trogg invasion, the contaminated runoff infiltrated the city's plumbing and aquifers. The trapped water elemental absorbed the deadly chemical stew, warping into an acidic, irradiated horror.",al={"why is it green","why is the elemental toxic","how was viscous fallout created"}},{q="Where in Gnomeregan does it wander?",a="Viscous Fallout patrols the lower irradiated passages and runoff canals below the main entry paths of Gnomeregan, often blending in among the ordinary mutated slimes and toxic wastes infesting the area.",al={"viscous fallout location","where to find viscous fallout","how to find viscous fallout"}},{q="Why is it hostile?",a="The elemental is driven mad by relentless agony and toxic corruption. Stripped of its natural purity, it lashes out furiously at any living creature trespassing in the tainted waterways.",al={"why does it attack","can it be saved"}},{q="Does it have any connection to Ironforge?",a="Gnomish refugees in Tinker Town inside Ironforge remember the complex waterways that once supported Gnomeregan. Items associated with the waterworks, such as the Hydrocane, are tied to these corrupted chambers and sought after for recovery.",al={"hydrocane ironforge","gnome connection"}},{q="Can the elemental be cleansed or cured?",a="No cure exists for the elemental. The radiation and toxic chemicals have permeated its form so entirely that destroying it is the only way to end its suffering.",al={"can you cure viscous fallout","cleanse viscous fallout"}}},ang={["race:Gnome"]="For gnomes, Viscous Fallout is a tragic reminder of the damage Mekgineer Thermaplugg inflicted upon their home, corrupting even the pristine subterranean springs that once sustained Gnomeregan.",["class:Shaman"]="A shaman will recognize the perversion of the elemental plane, seeing in Viscous Fallout a pure water spirit driven mad and defiled by artificial toxic waste.",["class:Druid"]="Druids view the creature as a living wound upon nature, illustrating the horrific consequences of reckless industrial contamination seeping into natural underground waters."},kw={"aquifer","gnomeregan","hydrocane","radiation","thermaplugg","tinker town","viscous fallout","water elemental"},rel={"zone:gnomeregan","subzone:tinker-town","zone:ironforge","topic:gnome","topic:druid"},src={"Viscous Fallout"}}
E["quest:2904"] = {t="quest",n="A Fine Mess",z="gnomeregan",s="Deep within the irradiated ruins of Gnomeregan, an injured gnome named Kernobee lies battered among troggs after being ambushed by Dark Iron dwarves. Rescuing him uncovers unsettling intelligence about Dark Iron involvement in subterranean drilling machinery, which must be relayed all the way to Booty Bay.",h="Deep within the irradiated ruins of Gnomeregan, an injured gnome named Kernobee lies battered among troggs...",sec={{t="A Battered Survivor",b="While navigating the dangerous inner chambers of Gnomeregan, adventurers discover Kernobee stranded in the dormitory area. Severely beaten and groggy, the gnome survived capture by Dark Iron dwarves who left him behind to perish among the feral troggs. Finding a friendly face is his only chance of surviving the trek back through the contaminated corridors.",sp=0},{t="Subterranean Schemes",b="Kernobee holds crucial information regarding dark forces operating beneath Dun Morogh. He reveals that the Dark Iron clan has actively involved itself in constructing a massive super rig. While Kernobee flees across the sea to Ratchet to warn the goblin engineer Tinkerwiz about this brewing threat, he sends his savior south to Booty Bay to deliver word to the goblin engineer Scooty.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Kernobee?",a="Kernobee is a gnome engineer who ventured deep into the ruins of Gnomeregan. He was ambushed, beaten nearly to death by Dark Iron dwarves, and abandoned to the troggs before being rescued.",al={"kernobee","who is kernobee","captured gnome"}},{q="Where must Kernobee be escorted?",a="Kernobee must be safely led through the hostile halls back toward the safety of the Clockwerk Run exit and the upper entrance corridors of the fallen city.",al={"where do i take kernobee","escort destination","clockwerk run exit"}},{q="Why were the Dark Iron dwarves involved?",a="The Dark Iron dwarves have been scheming underground, aiding in the design and construction of an enormous super rig drill. Kernobee discovered this plot before the dwarves ambushed him.",al={"why dark iron","dark iron super rig","dark iron in gnomeregan"}},{q="Where does Kernobee go after escaping?",a="After reaching safety, Kernobee heads across the sea to Ratchet in the Barrens to warn the tinker Tinkerwiz about the Dark Iron's involvement in the subterranean drilling rig.",al={"where did kernobee go","kernobee ratchet","tinkerwiz warning"},sp=1},{q="Why must you report to Scooty in Booty Bay?",a="Scooty is a goblin engineer stationed in Booty Bay who collaborates with Tinkerwiz and coordinates operations involving high-tech subterranean equipment and transponder networks.",al={"why scooty","booty bay turn in","scooty connection"}},{q="How does this relate to Mekgineer Thermaplugg?",a="Scooty recognizes the ongoing threat posed by Mekgineer Thermaplugg inside Gnomeregan. Helping Kernobee provides aid and supplies to adventurers intending to return and confront the treacherous Mekgineer.",al={"thermaplugg connection","fight thermaplugg"}}},ang={["race:Gnome"]="Rescuing a trapped brother from Gnomeregan's contaminated depths is a duty of honor, especially against the combined malice of Dark Iron infiltrators and feral troggs.",["faction:Alliance"]="Uncovering Dark Iron collusion within Dun Morogh's borders confirms that Emperor Thaurissan's agents are actively sabotaging Alliance recovery efforts in Gnomeregan.",["profession:Engineering"]="The discovery that Dark Iron machinists are constructing a massive super rig raises immediate concerns for any engineer tracking advanced subterranean hardware."},kw={"booty bay","clockwerk run","dark iron","gnomeregan","kernobee","scooty","super rig","tinkerwiz","troggs"},rel={"zone:gnomeregan","npc:kernobee","npc:scooty","subzone:clockwerk-run","subzone:dormitory","subzone:booty-bay","subzone:ratchet","topic:gnome"},m={start="Kernobee",["end"]="Scooty",level="30",id=2904},src={"A Fine Mess"}}
E["quest:2922"] = {t="quest",n="Save Techbot's Brain!",z="gnomeregan",s="Tinkmaster Overspark tasks Alliance adventurers with retrieving the memory core of Techbot from the irradiated ruins of Gnomeregan. The once-helpful mechanical assistant suffered severe brain polarization during the city's fall, causing it to run amok. Overspark hopes recovering its core will allow him to reverse the damage and restore his beloved creation.",h="Tinkmaster Overspark tasks Alliance adventurers with retrieving the memory core of Techbot from the...",sec={{t="A Mind Inverted",b="Before the disaster that claimed Gnomeregan, Techbot served as a marvel of gnomish ingenuity. Designed by Chief Architect Tinkmaster Overspark, the automaton aided researchers with countless integrated gizmos and an encyclopedic repository of technical knowledge. However, the chaos of the trogg invasion and the venting of toxic radiation did not spare the machine. A stray electrical surge jolted Techbot's delicate internal architecture, completely polarizing its positronic brain into a volatile negatronic state.",sp=0},{t="Salvage Operation",b="Trapped within the contaminated halls of Gnomeregan, Techbot now wanders in a manic frenzy, attacking anyone in sight. Despite its violent malfunction, Overspark refuses to write off his prized assistant as scrap. He recruits capable operatives to track down the berserk automaton, extract its memory core from the metal chassis, and deliver it safely to Ironforge so the Tinkmaster can unravel the polarization and repair Techbot's mind.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Techbot?",a="Techbot is a mechanical assistant invented by Tinkmaster Overspark. Prior to the fall of Gnomeregan, it assisted the Tinkmaster and his associates with its massive database of knowledge and built-in gizmos.",al={"what is techbot","techbot lore","overspark techbot"}},{q="Why did Techbot become hostile?",a="During the fall of Gnomeregan, a stray electrical spark jolted Techbot's positronic brain. The shock reversed its neural alignment into a negatronic state, turning its helpful personality into a rampaging frenzy.",al={"why is techbot mad","what happened to techbot","techbot polarization"}},{q="Where can Techbot be found?",a="Techbot wanders the outer corridors and staging halls of Gnomeregan, just beyond the perimeter lines where the exiled gnomes and dwarven expeditionary forces operate.",al={"where is techbot","techbot location","find techbot"}},{q="Who gives this quest?",a="Tinkmaster Overspark offers the quest from Tinker Town inside Ironforge, where he oversees salvage and research efforts on behalf of High Tinker Gelbin Mekkatorque.",al={"who starts save techbots brain","overspark location"}},{q="Can Techbot truly be repaired?",a="Tinkmaster Overspark believes retrieving Techbot's memory core will allow him to diagnose the exact cause of the negatronic polarization and restore the automaton to working order.",al={"is techbot fixed","can you fix techbot","does techbot survive"}},{q="What happens after returning the memory core?",a="Upon receiving the core, Overspark immediately sets to work preparing to dismantle and reconfigure the inverted circuits, though finding the right tools in his cluttered workshop proves to be its own challenge.",al={"techbot quest conclusion","turn in techbot core"},sp=1}},ang={["race:Gnome"]="For gnomish engineers, Techbot represents the tragic collateral damage of losing their home city, proving that even their finest intellectual achievements can be warped by the catastrophe.",["profession:Engineering"]="The transition of Techbot's processor from positronic to negatronic is a cautionary tale for tinkerers working with high-complexity computational matrices.",["faction:Alliance"]="Recovering valuable lost technology from within the contaminated perimeter of Gnomeregan is vital to supporting the gnomish refugees sheltering in Ironforge."},kw={"gnomeregan","memory core","negatronic","overspark","positronic","techbot","tinker town"},rel={"quest:2923","zone:gnomeregan","topic:gnome","zone:ironforge"},m={start="Tinkmaster Overspark",level="26",faction="Alliance",id=2922},src={"Save Techbot's Brain!"}}
E["quest:2923"] = {t="quest",n="Tinkmaster Overspark",z="gnomeregan",s="This errand directs Alliance adventurers in Stormwind to Tinker Town in Ironforge, where Chief Architect Tinkmaster Overspark is mourning a tragic malfunction. Brother Sarno sends word that Overspark's mechanical creation, Techbot, has gone rogue amidst the irradiated ruins of Gnomeregan. Reaching the Tinkmaster is the first step toward recovering the wayward construct's memory core.",h="This errand directs Alliance adventurers in Stormwind to Tinker Town in Ironforge, where Chief Architect...",sec={{t="A Plea from the Cathedral",b="Brother Sarno, tending to travelers in Stormwind City, shares word of an unfortunate dilemma brewing among the gnomish refugees. Tinkmaster Overspark—one of the brilliant minds behind Gnomeregan's wonders—is distraught over the corruption of Techbot, a once-helpful mechanical servant that served the tinkerers faithfully before the city fell into ruin.",sp=0},{t="To Tinker Town",b="The quest dispatches helpful souls via the Deeprun Tram up into Ironforge's bustling enclave of Tinker Town. There, Overspark desperately seeks adventurers brave enough to plunge back into the irradiated halls of Gnomeregan to salvage what remains of Techbot's faculties before the construct causes irreparable harm.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Tinkmaster Overspark?",a="Tinkmaster Overspark is the Chief Architect of Gnomeregan and High Tinker Gelbin Mekkatorque's foremost inventor. Currently stationed in Tinker Town within Ironforge, he works tirelessly to coordinate reclaim efforts and rescue stray gnomish technology from their ruined capital.",al={"overspark","who is overspark","tinkmaster overspark"}},{q="Who starts this quest?",a="Brother Sarno, a human cleric situated in Stormwind City, gives adventurers this quest to guide them toward the gnomes needing aid in Ironforge.",al={"quest giver","where to get tinkmaster overspark quest"}},{q="What is Techbot?",a="Techbot is a mechanical creation designed by Tinkmaster Overspark. Formerly a helpful and friendly tool for gnomish engineers, it malfunctioned following the catastrophic fall of Gnomeregan and went rogue in the irradiated city.",al={"techbot","what happened to techbot"}},{q="Where can Tinkmaster Overspark be found?",a="Overspark resides in Tinker Town, the gnomish quarter located in the eastern district of Ironforge, surrounded by fellow refugee tinkerers and experimental machinery.",al={"overspark location","where is overspark"}},{q="What follows after speaking to Overspark?",a="Upon reporting to Overspark, he offers the quest 'Save Techbot's Brain!', asking you to venture into Gnomeregan's outskirts to deactivate Techbot and retrieve its memory core so it can be restored.",al={"next quest","save techbot's brain"}},{q="Why is the Alliance interested in an inventor's broken machine?",a="Beyond sympathy for the exiled gnomes, wandering rogue automatons inside Gnomeregan present an immediate threat to any expeditions attempting to reclaim the underground capital or protect Dun Morogh's borders.",al={"why care about techbot","techbot importance"}}},ang={["race:Gnome"]="Every salvaged creation and recovered memory core represents a piece of your fallen homeland preserved before radiation and troggs destroyed it completely.",["profession:Engineering"]="Overspark's creations represent the cutting edge of gnomish ingenuity, making any opportunity to examine his rogue constructs an instructive endeavor.",["faction:Alliance"]="Aiding the displaced gnomish refugees in Tinker Town strengthens the vital bonds between Stormwind and the dwarven and gnomish kingdoms."},kw={"gnomeregan","ironforge","overspark","sarno","techbot","tinker town","tinkmaster"},rel={"npc:brother-sarno","quest:2922","subzone:tinker-town","zone:gnomeregan","zone:ironforge","topic:gnome"},m={start="Brother Sarno",["end"]="Tinkmaster Overspark",level="26",faction="Alliance",id=2923},src={"Tinkmaster Overspark (quest)"}}
E["quest:2924"] = {t="quest",n="Essential Artificials",z="gnomeregan",s="Essential Artificials is an Alliance quest offered by Klockmort Spannerspan in Ironforge's Tinker Town. Tasked with plumbing the depths of the irradiated ruins of Gnomeregan, adventurers must recover crucial universal components that were abandoned during the gnomes' desperate evacuation.",h="Essential Artificials is an Alliance quest offered by Klockmort Spannerspan in Ironforge's Tinker Town.",sec={{t="Forgotten in the Exodus",b="When the trogg invasion overwhelmed Gnomeregan and toxic radiation flooded its corridors, the fleeing gnomes could only carry what was immediately at hand. Among the countless marvels left behind were supplies of essential artificials—specialized, nigh-universal mechanical components prized by tinkers and crafters. Now operating out of Tinker Town in Ironforge, master tinker Klockmort Spannerspan finds his groundbreaking new experiments stalled without them.",sp=0},{t="Delving the Extrapolators",b="These vital devices are housed within heavy, steam-powered storage units known as artificial extrapolators located deep within the fallen city. Salvaging them requires braving irradiated halls crawling with mutated leper gnomes, malfunctioning defense automatons, and feral troggs. Recovering a cache of twelve components allows Klockmort to resume his critical work, pushing gnomish innovation forward despite their exile.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is an essential artificial?",a="An essential artificial is a nigh-universal mechanical component developed by gnomish engineers. Highly valued by tinkers and smiths, it serves as a critical building block for intricate contraptions and advanced experimental machinery.",al={"what are essential artificials","essential artificial","what is it"}},{q="Who gives the quest Essential Artificials?",a="The quest is given by Klockmort Spannerspan, a gnomish engineer located in Tinker Town within Ironforge.",al={"quest giver","who starts this","where do i get essential artificials"}},{q="Where are the essential artificials found in Gnomeregan?",a="They are stored deep inside Gnomeregan within containers called artificial extrapolators, which resemble tall, steam-powered cabinets or closets scattered throughout the lower halls.",al={"where are they","extrapolator location","how to find artificials"}},{q="Why were they left behind in Gnomeregan?",a="During the sudden trogg invasion and the subsequent radioactive catastrophe, the gnomes fled their capital in sheer panic. In the chaos of the evacuation, stockpiles of these crucial components were left behind in the lower workshops.",al={"why left behind","why are they in gnomeregan","lore of the artificials"}},{q="What does Klockmort need them for?",a="Klockmort Spannerspan requires a substantial supply of these universal components to fuel a series of new, complex experiments he is preparing to undertake from his workshop in Ironforge.",al={"why does klockmort want them","klockmort's plan"}},{q="Is Klockmort's Essentials required before taking this quest?",a="While the courier delivery quest 'Klockmort's Essentials' introduces you to Klockmort and directs you to his workshop, it is not a strict prerequisite for accepting Essential Artificials.",al={"prerequisite","prereq","klockmorts essentials required"}}},ang={["race:Gnome"]="Retrieving these components is a matter of national pride and technological continuity, ensuring that exile in Ironforge does not halt gnomish ingenuity.",["profession:Engineering"]="Every engineer understands the agony of missing a single universal component; recovering these devices highlights the sheer sophistication of pre-fall Gnomeregan craftsmanship.",["faction:Alliance"]="Assisting the exiled gnomes in reclaiming their lost tech strengthens the Alliance's technological backbone housed inside Ironforge."},kw={"artificial extrapolator","essential artificials","gnomeregan","gnomish engineering","ironforge","klockmort spannerspan","tinker town"},rel={"quest:1704","quest:2925","zone:gnomeregan","zone:ironforge","topic:gnome"},m={start="Klockmort Spannerspan",level="30",faction="Alliance",id=2924},src={"Essential Artificials"}}
E["quest:2925"] = {t="quest",n="Klockmort's Essentials",z="gnomeregan",s="Klockmort's Essentials is a summons carrying urgent word from the night elf Mathiel to his gnome friend, Klockmort Spannerspan. Unable to abandon his duties to travel to Dun Morogh, Mathiel enlists passing Alliance travelers to answer Klockmort's plea for help in Ironforge. The call directs adventurers into Tinkertown to prepare for a perilous venture into the irradiated halls of Gnomeregan.",h="Klockmort's Essentials is a summons carrying urgent word from the night elf Mathiel to his gnome friend...",sec={{t="A Call Across Continents",b="Word travels far even in troubled times. When Klockmort Spannerspan found himself in need of bold allies for a mission into Gnomeregan, he reached out across the sea to his night elf acquaintance, Mathiel. Mathiel, bound to his own post, cannot journey to the mountain kingdom himself, but he refuses to leave his friend's plea unanswered. Instead, he appeals to capable Alliance adventurers wandering through his encampment to make the trek to Dun Morogh on his behalf.",sp=0},{t="The Road to Tinkertown",b="Klockmort Spannerspan operates out of Tinkertown, the bustling refugee district of Ironforge where displaced gnomes have gathered since the catastrophic fall of their underground city. Amid the whir of gears and clouds of steam, Klockmort is formulating plans to retrieve vital machinery left behind in Gnomeregan's contaminated corridors. Taking Mathiel's referral leads adventurers directly to Klockmort's workshop, enlisting them in his reclamation efforts.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who gives the quest Klockmort's Essentials?",a="The quest is offered by Mathiel, a night elf who has received word from his gnome friend Klockmort Spannerspan. Mathiel cannot travel to Ironforge himself, so he asks trusted Alliance adventurers to go in his stead.",al={"quest giver","who starts klockmort essentials","mathiel quest"}},{q="Where do I find Klockmort Spannerspan?",a="Klockmort Spannerspan resides in Tinkertown, the gnomish sector of Ironforge. He is located among the workshops and refugee apparatuses set up by gnomes displaced from their lost home.",al={"where is klockmort","klockmort location","klockmort spannerspan ironforge"}},{q="Why does Klockmort need help in Gnomeregan?",a="Gnomeregan was overrun and irradiated by toxic fallout, leaving it crawling with troggs, deranged leper gnomes, and haywire automata. Klockmort requires intrepid adventurers to brave the hazards and retrieve essential mechanical components from within the ruins.",al={"what does klockmort want","why gnomeregan mission","klockmort purpose"}},{q="Is this quest required to enter Gnomeregan?",a="No, this quest is an optional breadcrumb leading you from Mathiel directly to Klockmort Spannerspan. You can speak to Klockmort in Ironforge and accept his dungeon assignments directly even without Mathiel's introduction.",al={"is this quest mandatory","prereq for gnomeregan","can i skip klockmort essentials"}},{q="What quest follows Klockmort's Essentials?",a="Speaking to Klockmort Spannerspan completes this errand and immediately leads into the quest Essential Artificials, which directs adventurers deep inside the dungeon of Gnomeregan.",al={"next quest","followup","essential artificials followup"}},{q="Why is Mathiel interested in helping a gnome in Ironforge?",a="Mathiel and Klockmort are long-time personal friends. Even though Mathiel is stationed far away and unable to abandon his current post, his concern for his friend drives him to find someone trustworthy to lend a hand.",al={"mathiel connection","why does mathiel care","mathiel and klockmort"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="This quest bridges the far reaches of Alliance territory, linking night elf lands with the dwarven mountain halls of Ironforge in common defense.",["race:Gnome"]="For gnomes, any errand directing adventurers to Tinkertown aids in the desperate, ongoing struggle to reclaim their lost home of Gnomeregan."},kw={"essential artificials","gnomeregan","ironforge","klockmort spannerspan","klockmort's essentials","leper gnomes","mathiel","tinkertown"},rel={"quest:1703","quest:2924","zone:gnomeregan","zone:ironforge","topic:gnome"},m={start="Mathiel",["end"]="Klockmort Spannerspan",level="30",faction="Alliance",id=2925},src={"Klockmort's Essentials"}}
E["quest:2926"] = {t="quest",n="Gnogaine",z="gnomeregan",s="Gnogaine is an Alliance quest offered by Ozzie Togglevolt in Kharanos. In an eccentric attempt to synthesize a cure for the leper gnomes—or perhaps concoct an extraordinarily potent beverage—Ozzie tasks adventurers with venturing toward Gnomeregan to gather radioactive fallout from glowing troggs.",h="Gnogaine is an Alliance quest offered by Ozzie Togglevolt in Kharanos.",sec={{t="A Cure or a Cocktail",b="Ever since the fall of Gnomeregan, refugees like Gnoarn have fixated entirely on exterminating the trogg invaders and reversing the radioactive affliction that mutated their brethren. In contrast, Ozzie Togglevolt and his partner Razzle Sprysprocket take a somewhat less orthodox approach from their workshop in Kharanos. While purporting to pursue a cure for the leper gnomes, Ozzie openly admits their experimental formula might just as easily end up being a recipe for remarkably strong rum.",sp=0},{t="Harvesting the Glow",b="To refine their concoction, the inventors require raw toxic residue directly from the epicenter of the catastrophe. Equipping adventurers with a leaden collection phial, Ozzie sends them toward the breached tunnels of Gnomeregan. There, roving irradiated invaders and pillagers—troggs saturated with leaking waste—glow with the sickening green energy needed to charge the flask.",sp=0},{t="Hair and High Hopes",b="Upon securing a full phial of green glow, Ozzie wastes no time preparing a live trial. Beyond hoping to restore sanity and health to a captured leper gnome, the tinkerer harbors personal aspirations for the brew, believing the fallout mixture might also miraculously cure his baldness.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who offers the quest Gnogaine?",a="The quest is given by Ozzie Togglevolt, a gnome tinkerer stationed in Kharanos within Dun Morogh.",al={"who gives gnogaine","gnogaine quest giver","ozzie togglevolt quest"}},{q="What do I need to collect for this quest?",a="You must use an Empty Leaden Collection Phial on glowing, irradiated troggs—specifically Irradiated Invaders or Irradiated Pillagers—found in the exterior corridors leading to Gnomeregan until the phial is filled with radioactive fallout.",al={"gnogaine objective","what do i collect gnogaine","full leaden collection phial"}},{q="Where can I find the irradiated troggs?",a="They are located in the outer entrance caverns and winding halls leading up to the Gnomeregan instance portal, allowing you to complete the task without stepping foot inside the dungeon itself.",al={"where are irradiated troggs","gnogaine trogg location","irradiated invader location"}},{q="Do I have to complete 'The Day After' before taking this quest?",a="No. While 'The Day After' is narratively tied to the situation in Kharanos and leads up to it, Ozzie will offer 'Gnogaine' independently.",al={"is the day after required","gnogaine prerequisite"}},{q="What is Ozzie trying to accomplish with the radioactive fallout?",a="Ozzie claims he and Razzle are attempting to create a cure for leper gnomes, though he admits the concoction might just turn out to be high-proof rum. He also privately hopes the concoction will restore his hair.",al={"why does ozzie want radiation","what is gnogaine for"}},{q="What quest follows Gnogaine?",a="Turning in the full phial leads directly to 'The Only Cure is More Green Glow', which requires venturing deeper into Gnomeregan itself.",al={"gnogaine follow up","what comes after gnogaine"}}},ang={["race:Gnome"]="For exiled gnomes, the desperation to find any remedy for their irradiated brethren makes even Ozzie's borderline-unhinged experiments worth attempting.",["faction:Alliance"]="The contamination spilling out of Gnomeregan threatens Dun Morogh as a whole, making any attempt to understand or neutralize the fallout vital to regional security.",["profession:Engineering"]="Handling raw radioactive runoff using shielded leaden phials showcases typical, high-risk gnomish field science in action."},kw={"gnoarn","gnogaine","gnomeregan","green glow","irradiated trogg","kharanos","leper gnome","ozzie togglevolt","phial","radiation"},rel={"npc:ozzie-togglevolt","quest:2927","quest:2962","zone:gnomeregan","subzone:kharanos","topic:leper-gnome","topic:trogg","topic:gnome"},m={start="Ozzie Togglevolt",level="27",faction="Alliance",id=2926},src={"Gnogaine"}}
E["quest:2927"] = {t="quest",n="The Day After",z="gnomeregan",s="The Day After is an Alliance quest that bridges the survivors outside Gnomeregan with researchers stationed in Dun Morogh. Gnoarn, lamenting the catastrophic radiation leak that cost him his legendary hair and his homeland, sends adventurers to assist Ozzie Togglevolt in Kharanos as he searches for a solution.",h="The Day After is an Alliance quest that bridges the survivors outside Gnomeregan with researchers stationed...",sec={{t="A Tragic Loss",b="Gnomeregan's downfall took a deeply personal toll on every survivor, and Gnoarn is no exception. A refugee lingering near the irradiated ruins, Gnoarn mourns not only the mechanical wonderland stolen by trogg invaders, but also his prized gnomefro—a glorious mane lost in an instant when a bolt of toxic fallout blasted him. Driven by lingering fury toward the troggs and a desperate hope to recover the city, he directs sympathetic travelers to colleagues who might still possess the scientific prowess to salvage what remains.",sp=0},{t="The Road to Kharanos",b="Rather than surrender to despair, Gnoarn points Alliance champions toward Kharanos, where inventive minds have begun tackling the fallout. Chief among them is Ozzie Togglevolt, working alongside his partner Razzle Sprysprocket. Ozzie remembers the horrifying moment of the catastrophe vividly, recalling how Gnoarn's locks fell out in clumps while madness and thirst for vengeance took hold. Now, in the relative safety of the snowbound town, Ozzie turns his engineering genius toward analyzing the contamination in hopes of finding an antidote.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Gnoarn?",a="Gnoarn is a gnome refugee found near Gnomeregan. Deeply embittered by the trogg invasion and the city's radioactive vent catastrophe, he is especially traumatized by the sudden loss of his once-proud gnomefro.",al={"gnoarn","bald gnome","who gives the day after"}},{q="Why does Gnoarn send you to Ozzie Togglevolt?",a="Gnoarn believes there might still be hope to save Gnomeregan. Ozzie Togglevolt and his partner Razzle are stationed in Kharanos, conducting research into the toxic radiation clinging to the city and attempting to engineer a cure.",al={"why go to ozzie","ozzie togglevolt quest","kharanos engineer"}},{q="What happened to Gnomeregan to cause this?",a="During a massive subterranean invasion by barbaric troggs, High Tinker Gelbin Mekkatorque was persuaded to vent radioactive toxic waste into the lower halls to eradicate them. The gambit failed tragically, mutating or killing countless gnomes and rendering the techno-city unlivable without wiping out the troggs.",al={"what happened to gnomeregan","why is gnomeregan irradiated","trogg invasion"}},{q="Where does this quest chain lead after reaching Ozzie?",a="Reporting to Ozzie unlocks the quest 'Gnogaine', where Ozzie asks you to gather radioactive fallout directly from the irradiated troggs and gnomes outside Gnomeregan to test experimental neutralizing mixtures.",al={"the day after follow up","what comes after the day after","next quest"}}},ang={["race:Gnome"]="For gnomes, Gnoarn's peculiar lament captures the mixture of profound tragedy, eccentric pride, and bitter vengeance felt by every refugee exiled from their wondrous capital.",["faction:Alliance"]="Alliance heroes assist Dun Morogh's gnomish thinkers in containing the bizarre biochemical disaster threatening the mountain realm.",["profession:Engineering"]="Ozzie Togglevolt's efforts highlight the trial-and-error approach gnomish tinkerers take when confronting runaway techno-disasters."},kw={"gnoarn","gnomefro","gnomeregan","kharanos","ozzie togglevolt","radiation leak","the day after","troggs"},rel={"npc:gnoarn","npc:ozzie-togglevolt","quest:2926","quest:2962","zone:gnomeregan","subzone:kharanos","topic:gnome","topic:trogg"},m={start="Gnoarn",["end"]="Ozzie Togglevolt",level="27",faction="Alliance",id=2927},src={"The Day After"}}
E["quest:2928"] = {t="quest",n="Gyrodrillmatic Excavationators",z="gnomeregan",s="Deep in the Dwarven District of Stormwind, Shoni the Shilent is preparing a fleet of massive tunneling machines intended for transit to Dun Morogh. Stalled by a shortage of mechanical parts, she dispatches adventurers into the irradiated ruins of Gnomeregan to harvest intact gears and innards from rogue automatons.",h="Deep in the Dwarven District of Stormwind, Shoni the Shilent is preparing a fleet of massive tunneling...",sec={{t="A Fleet in Need of Guts",b="In Stormwind's Dwarven District, gnomish engineers work tirelessly to support their displaced kin. Among them is Shoni the Shilent, who oversees an ambitious subterranean venture: a fleet of gyrodrillmatic excavationators destined for Dun Morogh. The project faces a critical bottleneck, as she lacks the necessary components to get the massive digging rigs operational.",sp=0},{t="Salvage in the Fallen City",b="Rather than forge new parts from scratch, Shoni looks directly to the source of gnomish high technology: the lost city of Gnomeregan. The ruins and surrounding tunnels crawl with malfunctioning defense bots, mechanical sentries, and clockwork laborers roaming unchecked. Venturers are sent to pry apart these rogue machines and haul two dozen bundles of robo-mechanical guts back to human lands.",sp=0},{t="A Monumental Undertaking",b="Bringing back two dozen mechanical guts provides enough scrap to patch together exactly one excavationator. With nearly four hundred machines remaining in her fleet, Shoni's dream of mass subterranean transport remains a monumental, agonizingly slow endeavor. Even so, every functioning machine represents a small step toward regaining ground lost in the cataclysm of Gnomeregan.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is a gyrodrillmatic excavationator?",a="They are heavy gnomish tunneling rigs or mole machines designed for subterranean excavation and transport. Shoni the Shilent is attempting to assemble an entire fleet of them to move people or supplies to Dun Morogh.",al={"gyrodrillmatic excavationators","what is excavationator","gnome drill"}},{q="Who is Shoni the Shilent?",a="Shoni is a gnomish engineer stationed in the Dwarven District of Stormwind. Despite her moniker, she is an outspoken and demanding overseer bent on repairing hundreds of mechanical diggers.",al={"shoni the shilent","shoni","who is shoni"}},{q="Why does Shoni need parts from Gnomeregan specifically?",a="Gnomeregan is overrun with hundreds of haywire automatons, clockwork servitors, and defensive mechs. Because standard manufacturing supply lines were severed when the city fell, these rogue bots are the richest available source of compatible gnomish spare parts.",al={"why gnomeregan parts","why robot guts","gnomeregan salvage"}},{q="Where are the Robo-Mechanical Guts found?",a="The salvageable guts can be scavenged from the mechanical sentries, clockwork constructs, and other hostiles wandering the corridors of Gnomeregan, both within the ruined facility and along its upper tunnel approaches.",al={"robo-mechanical guts","where to get guts","mechanical guts gnomeregan"}},{q="Does fixing one machine finish Shoni's fleet?",a="No. Two dozen mechanical guts are only enough to repair a single drill. Upon turning them in, Shoni notes that she still has 398 excavationators left to go.",al={"how many excavationators","shoni fleet size","how many drills"}},{q="Why is an excavation fleet being prepared for Dun Morogh?",a="Dun Morogh is the gnomes' ancestral home and the location of their fallen capital. Preparing heavy tunneling rigs offers a means to dig, clear debris, and support operations in the snow-covered mountain reaches.",al={"fleet to dun morogh","why dun morogh","excavators purpose"}}},ang={["race:Gnome"]="Every salvaged component brings Shoni's subterranean fleet closer to viability, keeping the dream of reclamation and industrial recovery alive from within Stormwind.",["profession:Engineering"]="Stripping high-precision clockwork innards from fallen Gnomeregan servitors offers a practical lesson in advanced gnomish design and heavy machinery repair.",["faction:Alliance"]="Supporting gnomish excavation logistics out of Stormwind strengthens the ties between human hosts and the exiled survivors working to reclaim their heritage."},kw={"dun morogh","dwarven district","excavationators","gnomeregan","gnomish engineering","gyrodrillmatic","robo-mechanical guts","shoni the shilent"},rel={"npc:shoni-the-shilent","zone:gnomeregan","zone:dunmorogh","topic:gnome","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},m={start="Shoni the Shilent",level="30",faction="Alliance",id=2928},src={"Gyrodrillmatic Excavationators"}}
E["quest:2930"] = {t="quest",n="Data Rescue",z="gnomeregan",s="When the gnomes evacuated their irradiated capital, massive archives of vital technical knowledge and records were left behind. Master Mechanic Castpipe in Ironforge recruits daring operatives to infiltrate Gnomeregan and retrieve a high-security Prismatic Punch Card. Navigating through layers of computerized clearance, couriers must punch their way through progressively fortified terminals deep within the ruined city.",h="When the gnomes evacuated their irradiated capital, massive archives of vital technical knowledge and records...",sec={{t="Lost Archives of the Underground",b="The sudden fall of Gnomeregan to troggs and deadly radiation forced the gnomish populace to abandon centuries of advanced research, schematics, and civic logs. Scattered throughout the technological corridors are Matrix Punchograph terminals, the automated data hubs that regulate security clearances and file storage. For exile leaders like Master Mechanic Castpipe, recovering these punch-encoded archives from the ruined depths represents one of the highest priorities of the refugee community in Tinker Town.",sp=0},{t="A Hierarchy of Perforations",b="Gnomish data protocol demands rigorous clearance before granting access to central mainframes. Operating the system requires starting with a basic White Punch Card found among the wreckage outside the inner gates. Inserting it into a Matrix Punchograph 3005-A in the Train Depot produces a Yellow card, which must then be carried into the Dormitory's 3005-B terminal for a Blue upgrade, advanced through model 3005-C for a Red card, and finally brought down into the Engineering Labs to encode the coveted Prismatic Punch Card.",sp=0},{t="Gnomish Levity in Binary",b="While Castpipe treats the quest as a matter of dire civic urgency, the actual punch cards feature binary data streams that reveal the eccentric, irreverent mindset of Gnomeregan's computing guilds. Amid genuine technical data, the punch patterns translate into humorous quips, absurd workplace complaints, and off-color jokes about High Tinker Gelbin Mekkatorque wearing night elven undergarments—demonstrating that even in the heart of high-tech infrastructure, gnome engineers could never resist a practical joke.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is the Prismatic Punch Card?",a="The Prismatic Punch Card is the highest tier of security data card recognized by Gnomeregan's automated mainframes. It is created by processing a Red Punch Card at the Matrix Punchograph 3005-D terminal located deep inside the Engineering Labs.",al={"prismatic card","what is punch card","gnomeregan punch card"}},{q="Where does the sequence of punch cards begin?",a="The sequence begins with a basic White Punch Card, salvaged from troggs and mechanical derelicts lingering just outside the main instance entrance, near the Train Depot.",al={"where to get white punch card","how to start punch cards","first punch card"}},{q="Where are the Matrix Punchograph terminals located?",a="Model 3005-A stands outside the instance in the Train Depot. Model 3005-B rests inside the Dormitory past the Clean Zone. Model 3005-C is situated on the catwalk platforms beyond, while Model 3005-D sits on the lower level of the Engineering Labs.",al={"terminal locations","where are punchographs","punch card machines"}},{q="Who is Master Mechanic Castpipe?",a="Master Mechanic Castpipe is a senior gnome engineer living among the refugees in Ironforge's Tinker Town. Desperate to salvage Gnomeregan's intellectual heritage, he coordinates reconnaissance and retrieval missions into the fallen capital.",al={"castpipe","who gives data rescue","castpipe lore"}},{q="What data is actually on the cards?",a="When translated from raw ASCII binary, the punch cards contain a mixture of gnomish engineering banter, lighthearted jokes about regional leaders like Thrall and Mekkatorque, and eccentric notes alongside the city's critical computational data.",al={"card text","binary translation","what does the binary say"}},{q="Can Horde players access these terminals?",a="The quest itself is offered exclusively to the Alliance by Master Mechanic Castpipe in Ironforge, though the physical punchograph terminals inside the dungeon can technically be interfaced with by anyone carrying the requisite cards.",al={"horde data rescue","horde punch cards","can horde use terminals"}}},ang={["race:Gnome"]="Retrieving data from Gnomeregan represents reclaiming stolen heritage. Every punch card salvaged ensures that the ingenuity of your fallen city is preserved rather than lost to troggs and radiation.",["profession:Engineering"]="The Matrix Punchograph network showcases automated data storage at its finest, demonstrating intricate algorithmic clearance mechanisms devised by the Tinkers' Court.",["faction:Alliance"]="Supporting Castpipe's retrieval efforts aids the displaced gnomish government in Ironforge, strengthening unity and technological capabilities among the Grand Alliance."},kw={"castpipe","data rescue","engineering labs","gnomeregan","matrix punchograph","prismatic punch card","punch card","tinker town","train depot"},rel={"quest:2931","zone:gnomeregan","zone:ironforge","topic:gnome","subzone:train-depot","subzone:dormitory","subzone:engineering-labs","subzone:clean-zone"},m={start="Master Mechanic Castpipe",level="30",faction="Alliance",id=2930},src={"Data Rescue"}}
E["quest:2931"] = {t="quest",n="Castpipe's Task",z="gnomeregan",s="Castpipe's Task is an Alliance summons directing capable adventurers to seek out Master Mechanic Castpipe in Ironforge. Castpipe is coordinating perilous salvage operations into the irradiated ruins of Gnomeregan to extract vital mechanical and technical records. It serves as an official briefing that points mercenaries toward deep-retrieval missions inside the fallen city.",h="Castpipe's Task is an Alliance summons directing capable adventurers to seek out Master Mechanic Castpipe in...",sec={{t="A Call to Tinkertown",b="Following the tragic fall and subsequent radioactive quarantine of Gnomeregan, the surviving gnomes took refuge in Ironforge's Tinkertown. While their grand home remains overrun by troggs and irradiated constructs, crucial operational records and mechanical schematics are trapped deep within the city's surviving computing arrays. Recognizing that these files could prove invaluable to reclaiming or understanding what went wrong, Master Mechanic Castpipe began actively enlisting intrepid outsiders willing to brave the toxic halls.",sp=0},{t="Assembly Endorsement",b="Word of Castpipe's venture is spread by figures like Gaxim Rustfizzle of the Enlightened Assembly of Arcanology, Alchemy and Engineering Sciences. Though Castpipe is not a member of this esteemed academic body himself, fellow gnomes respect his technical acumen enough to endorse the effort. Rustfizzle's own calculations put the likelihood of Castpipe's mission having true strategic value at an encouraging eighty-four percent, motivating travelers to report to Tinkertown for orders.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Master Mechanic Castpipe?",a="Master Mechanic Castpipe is a respected gnomish engineer based in Tinkertown within Ironforge. He organizes salvage teams and data recovery operations focused on the subterranean ruins of Gnomeregan.",al={"castpipe","who is castpipe","master mechanic castpipe"}},{q="Why does Castpipe want data from Gnomeregan?",a="When Gnomeregan was contaminated and evacuated, vast amounts of critical technical knowledge, blueprints, and internal system logs were left behind in the mainframe memory. Retrieving this information is vital for the displaced gnomes hoping to rebuild.",al={"gnomeregan data","why retrieve data","gnomeregan records"}},{q="Who is Gaxim Rustfizzle?",a="Gaxim Rustfizzle is a gnome scholar affiliated with the Enlightened Assembly of Arcanology, Alchemy and Engineering Sciences. He acts as an advocate and liaison, directing capable adventurers toward Castpipe's recovery efforts.",al={"gaxim","rustfizzle"}},{q="Where can Castpipe be found?",a="Master Mechanic Castpipe is stationed in Tinkertown, the gnome-settled district in the northwestern quarter of the dwarven capital city of Ironforge.",al={"castpipe location","where is castpipe"}},{q="What happens after reporting to Castpipe?",a="Reporting to Master Mechanic Castpipe leads directly into a mission within the fallen city itself, known as Data Rescue, where adventurers must penetrate Gnomeregan's contaminated interior to extract computer punch cards and storage media.",al={"next quest","what comes next","after castpipe"}},{q="What is the Enlightened Assembly of Arcanology, Alchemy and Engineering Sciences?",a="The Enlightened Assembly of Arcanology, Alchemy and Engineering Sciences is a prestigious gnomish intellectual society dedicated to rigorous scientific, magical, and mechanical study. Its members, such as Gaxim Rustfizzle, apply rigorous probability to evaluate critical tasks.",al={"the assembly","enlightened assembly"}}},ang={["race:Gnome"]="Every recovery operation represents a fragment of your fallen home preserved from radiation and destruction, making Castpipe's mission a matter of cultural survival.",["profession:Engineering"]="The data cores inside Gnomeregan hold computational marvels and advanced schematics unmatched anywhere else on Azeroth.",["faction:Alliance"]="Assisting the displaced gnomish allies in securing their lost archives helps stabilize Tinkertown and strengthens the Alliance's collective technological standing."},kw={"assembly","castpipe","data rescue","gaxim","gnomeregan","ironforge","rustfizzle","tinkertown"},rel={"quest:2930","npc:gaxim-rustfizzle","zone:gnomeregan","zone:ironforge","topic:gnome"},m={start="Gaxim Rustfizzle",["end"]="Master Mechanic Castpipe",level="28",faction="Alliance",id=2931},src={"Castpipe's Task"}}
E["quest:2945"] = {t="quest",n="Grime-Encrusted Ring",z="gnomeregan",s="Deep within the irradiated ruins of Gnomeregan, adventurers can recover a jewelry piece heavily caked in toxic filth and hardened muck from a Dark Iron dwarf invader. Discovering its true identity requires using the Sparklematic 5200, an industrial cleaning automaton found inside the Dormitory sector. Once scrubbed clean, the ring reveals personal markings that launch a journey to return or refashion the heirloom.",h="Deep within the irradiated ruins of Gnomeregan, adventurers can recover a jewelry piece heavily caked in...",sec={{t="A Relic Beneath the Muck",b="Gnomeregan's corridors are swimming in toxic sludge, oil, and radioactive fallout, so it is no surprise that items dropped in the fighting become coated in impenetrable sludge. Slain Dark Iron dwarves infiltrating the city often carry heavily soiled trinkets, chief among them this grime-encrusted band. The crust is far too tough for mundane hand-washing, completely obscuring whether the metal beneath is copper, gold, or junk.",sp=0},{t="The Sparklematic 5200",b="To clean the ring, one must find the Sparklematic 5200 in the Clean Zone dormitory. Gnomish engineering at its most delightfully absurd, the machine accepts coins, subjects heavily fouled items to violent internal scouring, and spits them out freshly polished and neatly gift-wrapped with a bow. Stripping away the irradiated muck reveals an engraved insignia belonging to a citizen of Ironforge, turning a scavenged trinket into a quest of restitution.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where do you find the Grime-Encrusted Ring?",a="The Grime-Encrusted Ring is recovered from the corpses of Dark Iron dwarves encountered inside the besieged dungeon of Gnomeregan.",al={"ring drop","where does grime ring drop","who drops grime encrusted ring"}},{q="How do you clean the ring?",a="Take the ring to the Sparklematic 5200, located in the Clean Zone dormitory inside Gnomeregan. Inserting the ring along with the required coin fee will initiate an intense automated scrub that strips away the hardened muck.",al={"clean ring","how to clean grime encrusted ring","where to wash ring"}},{q="What happens after the ring is cleaned?",a="The Sparklematic dispenses a neatly packaged box containing a restored ring with distinct personal engravings. This begins the quest Return of the Ring, leading you to find its original owner.",al={"next quest grime ring","what do i do with clean ring","sparklematic ring result"}},{q="Can Horde players complete this quest?",a="Yes. Horde adventurers can use the Sparklematic 5200 to clean the ring. However, subsequent steps in the chain diverge, ultimately directing Horde players to an engineer in Orgrimmar rather than returning it to Ironforge.",al={"is grime ring alliance only","horde grime encrusted ring","can horde clean ring"}},{q="Why is the ring wrapped in a gift box after cleaning?",a="The Sparklematic 5200 is built with typical gnomish whimsy. In addition to vigorously scouring away sludge and grime, the apparatus is programmed to automatically package and tie a decorative bow around processed items upon completion.",al={"gift wrapped ring","why gift box sparklematic"}},{q="Are there multiple Sparklematic machines?",a="Several Sparklematic units line the wall in the Clean Zone dormitory, but only one functional machine is set up to clean quest items like the ring; the others primarily serve as repeatable salvage scrubbers for loose grime.",al={"which sparklematic","sparklematic 5200 locations"}}},ang={["profession:Engineering"]="The Sparklematic 5200 is a classic example of quirky gnomish engineering, combining industrial solvent-scrubbing with an automated gift-wrapping dispenser.",["race:Gnome"]="Even during the catastrophic fall of their city, gnomes designed sanitation contraptions that finish dangerous industrial wash cycles with a cheerful bell chime and a bow.",["race:Dwarf"]="The ring's presence on an infiltrating Dark Iron dwarf hints at scavenged loot taken from Ironforge or gnomish victims during the chaos of Gnomeregan's fall."},kw={"clean zone","dark iron","dormitory","gnomeregan","grime-encrusted ring","return of the ring","sparklematic 5200"},rel={"quest:2947","quest:2948","quest:2950","npc:nogg","zone:gnomeregan","topic:gnome"},m={start="Grime-Encrusted Ring",["end"]="Sparklematic 5200",id=2945},src={"Grime-Encrusted Ring (quest)"}}
E["quest:2947"] = {t="quest",n="Return of the Ring",z="gnomeregan",s="After scouring away layers of subterranean sludge in Gnomeregan's automated cleaning apparatus, an adventurer uncovers a pristine golden ring bearing the seal of Ironforge and the initials 'TdK'. Tracing those markings leads up to the bustling artisan alleys of the dwarven capital to locate its eccentric creator.",h="After scouring away layers of subterranean sludge in Gnomeregan's automated cleaning apparatus, an adventurer...",sec={{t="A Sludge-Coated Treasure",b="Deep within the irradiated ruins of Gnomeregan, ancient machinery still whirs in defiance of the trogg invasion. Feeding a grimy, caked bauble into the Sparklematic 5200 strips away years of irradiated toxic grime, revealing a polished Brilliant Gold Ring thrumming with arcane potency. Stamped along its inner band is the distinct hallmark seal of Ironforge, alongside three neatly engraved initials: 'TdK'.",sp=0},{t="The Artisan of the Mystic Ward",b="Those initials belong to none other than Talvash del Kissel, an eccentric gnome jeweler who operates out of Ironforge's Mystic Ward—often while frantically fending off imaginary debt collectors. Talvash quickly recognizes the craftsmanship as one of his standard, pre-fall designs from his old shop in Gnomeregan. Learning that the trinket was found in the clutches of Dark Iron infiltrators deeply rattles the craftsman, hinting at shadowy intrigues swirling beneath the lost tech-city.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who made the ring found in Gnomeregan?",a="The initials 'TdK' belong to Talvash del Kissel, a quirky gnome jeweler currently residing in the Mystic Ward of Ironforge. Before the fall of Gnomeregan, Talvash ran a jewelry shop inside the city and forged several simple magical rings of that design.",al={"who made the ring","ring initials tdk","who is tdk"}},{q="Where did the ring originally come from?",a="The ring was discovered as a grime-encrusted bauble deep within Gnomeregan, carried by hostile invaders like the Dark Iron dwarves. After running it through the automated Sparklematic 5200, its golden sheen and maker's marks were restored.",al={"where was ring found","where does ring come from"}},{q="Why were Dark Iron dwarves carrying Talvash's ring?",a="Talvash isn't entirely sure, but he notes that finding his pre-fall handiwork on Dark Iron infiltrators adds another suspicious layer to the conspiracies surrounding Gnomeregan's downfall. It likely came from his abandoned workshop or was looted from someone who failed to escape the invasion.",al={"why do dark irons have it","dark iron ring lore"}},{q="Why does Talvash del Kissel think you are his landlord?",a="Talvash is notoriously high-strung, eccentric, and chronically behind on his rent in Ironforge. Whenever strangers approach his shop aggressively, he assumes they are bailiffs or landlords coming to collect his overdue debts.",al={"why is talvash paranoid","talvash rent"}},{q="Does Talvash make cursed jewelry?",a="Talvash adamantly proclaims to all prospective customers that he does not make cursed items, though his nervous, preemptive denials tend to raise more questions than they answer.",al={"is talvash cursed","cursed jewelry ironforge"}},{q="Can I just keep the ring instead of returning it?",a="While the bauble possesses magical properties on its own, showing it to its creator allows Talvash to inspect the piece and offer to refine its enchantment further through subsequent work.",al={"keep the ring","should i return the ring"}}},ang={["race:Gnome"]="Recovering lost handiwork from the fallen city offers a rare glimpse into the peaceful everyday craft gnomes enjoyed before Thermaplugg's disaster.",["faction:Alliance"]="The discovery of Ironforge-marked artifacts in the hands of Dark Iron infiltrators reinforces the growing threat Emperor Thaurissan's agents pose to the Alliance's mountain home."},kw={"brilliant gold ring","dark iron","ironforge seal","mystic ward","sparklematic","talvash del kissel","tdk"},rel={"npc:talvash-del-kissel","quest:2945","quest:2948","zone:gnomeregan","zone:ironforge","topic:gnome","topic:alliance"},m={start="Sparklematic 5200",["end"]="Talvash del Kissel",faction="Alliance",id=2947},src={"Return of the Ring (Alliance)"}}
E["quest:2949"] = {t="quest",n="Return of the Ring",z="gnomeregan",s="After scouring away the filth of Gnomeregan in the Sparklematic 5200, an adventurer uncovers a ring bearing the seal of Orgrimmar and the engraved letters 'NOG'. Tracing the piece back to the Horde's capital leads directly to the goblin engineer Nogg, who has his own curious theories about the city's fall.",h="After scouring away the filth of Gnomeregan in the Sparklematic 5200, an adventurer uncovers a ring bearing...",sec={{t="A Curious Discovery",b="Gnomeregan is an Alliance city deep in Khaz Modan, making the recovery of a ring bearing the official seal of Orgrimmar entirely unexpected. Once processed through the gnomes' Sparklematic cleaning rig, the bauble sheds its thick layer of subterranean sludge, revealing a surge of magical power and the partially legible letters 'NOG'. Whether crafted in Kalimdor or brought along on an ill-fated expedition, the trinket clearly has roots in the Horde capital.",sp=0},{t="Gnomish Rivalries and Dark Iron Plots",b="Taking the ring back to the Valley of Honor in Orgrimmar leads straight to Nogg, an engineer who quickly clarifies that while the ring is not his personal jewelry, its origins raise intriguing questions. Bilgewater and Horde goblins have long looked down on gnomish inventors as eccentric rivals. To Nogg, the fact that Dark Iron dwarves held the ring inside Gnomeregan suggests the gnomes may have stolen advanced golem designs from the Dark Irons, sparking a retaliatory sabotage that ultimately doomed the city.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why does a ring found in Gnomeregan bear the seal of Orgrimmar?",a="The exact circumstances of how the ring entered Gnomeregan remain unknown, but it was carried deep into the ruins and recovered by Dark Iron dwarves. Its Orgrimmar insignia connects it back to Horde metalworkers and craftsmen operating out of Durotar.",al={"why orgrimmar seal","horde ring in gnomeregan","how did the ring get there"}},{q="Who is Nogg?",a="Nogg is a goblin engineer located in the Valley of Honor in Orgrimmar. He oversees engineering supplies and machines, and his name matches the worn letters engraved alongside the Orgrimmar seal on the cleaned ring.",al={"who is nogg","nogg orgrimmar","nog letters ring"}},{q="What is the Sparklematic 5200?",a="The Sparklematic 5200 is an automated industrial wash system located within the Clean Zone of Gnomeregan. It strips away heavy layers of toxic sludge and irradiation from objects dragged out of the ruined corridors.",al={"what is the sparklematic","sparklematic 5200","cleanomatic"}},{q="Does Nogg own the ring?",a="No. When presented with the cleaned band, Nogg inspects it and admits that it does not belong to him. However, he recognizes its craftsmanship and uses his engineering expertise to modify it further for the adventurer.",al={"is it nogg's ring","did nogg lose his ring","who owns the ring"},sp=1},{q="What does Nogg think happened to Gnomeregan?",a="Nogg suspects that the gnomes stole advanced golem blueprints from the Dark Iron clan. He believes the Dark Irons sought vengeance, insinuating that their clandestine meddling may have contributed directly to Gnomeregan's catastrophic downfall.",al={"nogg gnomeregan theory","what happened to gnomeregan","why dark iron dwarves"}},{q="Can I keep the ring instead of returning it to Nogg?",a="The choice is yours to wear the ring immediately or take it to Orgrimmar. Bringing it to Nogg, however, allows the goblin engineer to inspect its craftsmanship and offer further improvements.",al={"keep brilliant gold ring","should i return the ring","do i have to give it to nogg"}}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="Finding Horde iconography deep inside the premier technological capital of the Eastern Kingdoms is a rare sight, drawing Horde adventurers straight from Khaz Modan back to the Valley of Honor.",["profession:Engineering"]="The goblin engineers in Orgrimmar constantly measure themselves against gnomish invention, and Nogg is eager to dissect anything retrieved from the heart of their fallen technological wonder."},kw={"brilliant gold ring","dark iron","gnomeregan","nogg","orgrimmar","return of the ring","sparklematic 5200","valley of honor"},rel={"npc:nogg","zone:gnomeregan","zone:orgrimmar","quest:2945","quest:2950","topic:horde","topic:gnome"},m={start="The Sparklematic 5200",["end"]="Nogg",faction="Horde",id=2949},src={"Return of the Ring (Horde)"}}
E["quest:2951"] = {t="quest",n="The Sparklematic 5200!",z="gnomeregan",s="Deep within the ruins of Gnomeregan, the Sparklematic 5200 is an automated cleaning device that continues to function amidst the chaos. By feeding it a grime-encrusted object scavenged from the subterranean halls along with a nominal coin fee, adventurers can restore salvaged trinkets, gems, and scrap to pristine condition. It stands as a vibrant testament to the enduring ingenuity and eccentricity of gnomish engineering.",h="Deep within the ruins of Gnomeregan, the Sparklematic 5200 is an automated cleaning device that continues to...",sec={{t="A Beacon in the Grime",b="Amidst the radioactive fallback and trogg infestation consuming Gnomeregan, a pocket of surviving gnomes maintains a secure perimeter near an extraordinary invention: the Sparklematic 5200. Built to scrub the harsh subterranean filth off salvaged valuables, this sturdy contraption promises to put the 'shine back in shine-tastic.' Even while subterranean monstrosities pound on the bulkheads, the machine sits ready for commercial operation.",sp=0},{t="Frenzied Operation",b="The cleaning mechanism is anything but gentle. Once an adventurer deposits a grime-caked relic alongside three silver coins, the Sparklematic surges into a violent, churning frenzy. The entire iron apparatus groans, vibrates, and lurches from side to side as it strips away toxic sludge, irradiated grease, and rock dust. Moments later, it expels whatever was buried beneath the muck, ranging from precious minerals to mechanical components.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Sparklematic 5200?",a="The Sparklematic 5200 is an automated gnomish cleaning contraption stationed within the safe pocket of Gnomeregan. It is designed to strip stubborn radioactive grease, sludge, and dirt off encrusted items recovered throughout the fallen city.",al={"what does sparklematic 5200 do","sparklematic machine","cleaning machine gnomeregan"}},{q="What does the machine require to operate?",a="Operating the Sparklematic requires a Grime-Encrusted Object found among the monsters and debris of Gnomeregan, as well as a processing fee of three silver coins deposited directly into the machine's coin slot.",al={"how to use sparklematic","sparklematic cost","what do i put in sparklematic"}},{q="Why is there an operational machine in the middle of a war zone?",a="Gnomish civilization was built around automated domestic and industrial convenience. When the trogg invasion and toxic vents devastated the city, surviving gnomes fell back into fortified workshops where machines like the Sparklematic remained intact and powered.",al={"why is sparklematic here","who put sparklematic in gnomeregan"}},{q="What comes out after cleaning a grime-encrusted item?",a="The machine returns your salvaged item completely purged of filth, revealing useful trade supplies, crafting stones, gems, or spare engineering parts that were buried beneath the muck.",al={"what do you get from sparklematic","sparklematic loot","grime-encrusted object rewards"}},{q="Can I use the Sparklematic 5200 more than once?",a="Yes. After the initial demonstration runs, the contraption can be used repeatedly via ongoing cleaning tasks as long as you provide additional grime-encrusted objects and silver coins.",al={"is sparklematic repeatable","can i clean multiple grime items","more sparklematic"}},{q="Why does the machine shake so violently during cleaning?",a="The encrusted filth within Gnomeregan is dense, toxic, and hardened. The machine relies on high-velocity agitation and internal scrubbers to shear the grime away, causing the entire chassis to lurch and groan during operation.",al={"sparklematic shaking","is sparklematic broken"}}},ang={["race:Gnome"]="The machine reflects classic gnomish resilience: even during a catastrophic homeland evacuation, commerce and sparkling cleanliness march on without interruption.",["profession:Engineering"]="Engineers can appreciate the robust motor and sorting architecture required to cleanse and process unknown debris without jamming or exploding.",["faction:Alliance"]="For Alliance salvage teams braving Gnomeregan's halls, the machine provides an immediate way to clean scavenged relics before carrying them back to Ironforge."},kw={"cleaner","gnome","gnomeregan","grime-encrusted","machine","salvage","sparklematic","sparklematic 5200","trogg"},rel={"quest:2953","zone:gnomeregan","topic:gnome"},m={start="The Sparklematic 5200",faction="Neutral",id=2951},src={"The Sparklematic 5200! (1)"}}
E["quest:2952"] = {t="quest",n="The Sparklematic 5200!",z="gnomeregan",s="Deep within the irradiated halls of Gnomeregan sits the Sparklematic 5200, an automated cleaning contraption designed to scrub toxic filth from recovered salvaging. Operating the machine strips heavy grime from soiled objects and packages whatever is salvaged in a decorative gift box.",h="Deep within the irradiated halls of Gnomeregan sits the Sparklematic 5200, an automated cleaning contraption...",sec={{t="Automated Cleansing",b="Gnomish engineering often prizes efficiency and whimsy in equal measure. The Sparklematic 5200 was built to handle toxic and contaminated refuse, scouring away grime and caustic residue through automated cycles. Once loaded and paid, the contraption rattles through its cleaning routine before emitting a cheerful ding, neatly wrapping whatever remains into a present tied with a bow.",sp=0},{t="Treasure in the Sludge",b="Since the fall of Gnomeregan to the troggs and the subsequent radiation disaster, countless personal effects and technological scraps were smothered in industrial mire. Adventurers who feed grime-encrusted objects into the machine can reclaim lost gemstones, raw ores, and long-lost valuables that were swallowed up when the city was vented.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What does the Sparklematic 5200 do?",a="The Sparklematic 5200 is an automated cleaning machine inside Gnomeregan. When supplied with a grime-encrusted object and a coin fee, it cleans away sludge, grime, and radioactive muck, returning the cleaned contents packaged in a small gift box.",al={"what is sparklematic 5200","how sparklematic works","sparklematic function"}},{q="Where is the Sparklematic 5200 located?",a="The machine is located inside the interior corridors of the fallen city of Gnomeregan, near the Clean Zone where survivors and automated decontamination systems once operated.",al={"sparklematic location","where is the cleaning machine","find sparklematic"}},{q="Why does the machine wrap items in a bow?",a="It was programmed with typical gnomish whimsy. Even after scrubbing dangerous fallout and toxic grime off an item, its creators designed the finishing cycle to package the restored object into a pleasant, neatly tied present.",al={"why gift box","sparklematic wrapped present","wrapped in bow"}},{q="Can Horde adventurers use the Sparklematic 5200?",a="Yes. The Sparklematic 5200 is a fully automated apparatus that does not care about faction allegiances. So long as a visitor inserts coins and soiled items, the machine runs its cycle.",al={"horde sparklematic","can horde clean grime","is sparklematic neutral"}},{q="Can I use the Sparklematic multiple times?",a="Yes. After the initial operation, the machine unlocks a repeatable task allowing anyone who discovers grime-encrusted items throughout the dungeon to process them again and again.",al={"is sparklematic repeatable","more sparklematic action","farm grime encrusted objects"}},{q="What happens after this quest?",a="Completing this initial cleansing leads directly to the repeatable cleaning cycle known as More Sparklematic Action, allowing you to clean any additional grime-encrusted finds you carry.",al={"next quest after sparklematic","what follows sparklematic 5200"}}},ang={["race:Gnome"]="The Sparklematic is a stark reminder of home before the fall: even an industrial scrub unit had to chime cheerfully and deliver the finished product wrapped up like a birthday present.",["profession:Engineering"]="Studying the Sparklematic offers a look at automated particulate cleaning and rapid packaging mechanisms engineered to endure heavy ambient radiation."},kw={"cleaning","contraption","decontamination","gnomeregan","grime","machine","sparklematic"},rel={"quest:2951","quest:2953","zone:gnomeregan"},m={start="The Sparklematic 5200",faction="Neutral",id=2952},src={"The Sparklematic 5200! (2)"}}
E["quest:2953"] = {t="quest",n="More Sparklematic Action",z="gnomeregan",s="Deep within the irradiated ruins of Gnomeregan stands the Sparklematic 5200, an automated cleaning apparatus left behind during the city's evacuation. For a small fee of silver, this machine vigorously scrubs salvageable curiosities from the muck and radioactive sludge coating the fallen capital.",h="Deep within the irradiated ruins of Gnomeregan stands the Sparklematic 5200, an automated cleaning apparatus...",sec={{t="Automated Restoration",b="The Sparklematic 5200 represents the ingenious automated infrastructure gnomes installed throughout Gnomeregan before the trogg invasion and subsequent fallout. Even with toxic waste and hostile automatons filling the corridors, this contraption still performs its exact programming whenever provided with three silver coins and a grime-encrusted artifact.",sp=0},{t="Wonders from the Muck",b="When engaged, the Sparklematic lurches wildly while dousing and scrubbing the inserted relic in potent gnomish cleaning solvents. Once the cycle finishes with a cheerful chime, it dispenses a neatly packaged box containing whatever salvage was preserved beneath the corrosive trogg slime and toxic filth.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Sparklematic 5200?",a="The Sparklematic 5200 is an automated gnomish cleaning device situated inside Gnomeregan. It strips caustic sludge, grime, and radioactive detritus from recovered objects, restoring them into identifiable salvage.",al={"sparklematic 5200","what does the machine do","gnomeregan cleaner"}},{q="Why does the machine charge coins?",a="Gnomish infrastructure frequently relies on coin-operated automated service models to offset mechanical maintenance and chemical replenishment costs, requiring three silver coins to trigger its internal cleaning sequence.",al={"why pay silver","sparklematic cost"}},{q="What kinds of objects can be put inside?",a="The machine specifically cleans grime-encrusted objects, relics recovered from fallen troggs, corrupted sentries, and irradiated horrors wandering the tunnels of Gnomeregan.",al={"grime-encrusted object","what items can i clean"}},{q="Is the Sparklematic safe from radiation?",a="While the exterior tunnels are steeped in radioactive waste, the Sparklematic 5200 remains functional, deploying specialized gnomish cleaning agents to scrub dangerous exterior residue off incoming objects.",al={"sparklematic irradiated","sparklematic contamination"}},{q="Can both factions use the Sparklematic 5200?",a="Yes. The Sparklematic 5200 is a completely mechanical, automated installation that operates neutrally, accepting payment and grime-encrusted items regardless of the visitor's allegiance.",al={"horde sparklematic","who can use it"}},{q="Who designed the Sparklematic?",a="It was designed by Gnomeregan's municipal engineers prior to the city's fall, built as an easy, automated amenity for citizens and technicians handling muddy or contaminated machinery.",al={"sparklematic creator","who built sparklematic"}}},ang={["race:Gnome"]="The Sparklematic is a testament to gnomish mechanical endurance, functioning reliably amidst the toxic ruins of your homeland.",["profession:Engineering"]="Operating the device gives engineers a firsthand look at robust gnomish solvent cycles and coin-activated automation."},kw={"automation","clean machine","cleaning","gnomeregan","grime-encrusted","sparklematic"},rel={"quest:2951","zone:gnomeregan"},m={start="Sparklematic 5200",faction="Neutral",id=2953},src={"More Sparklematic Action"}}
E["quest:2962"] = {t="quest",n="The Only Cure is More Green Glow",z="gnomeregan",s="Following earlier inconclusive tests on surface troggs, Ozzie Togglevolt tasks adventurers with retrieving pure, high-potency radioactive fallout directly from inside Gnomeregan. His ultimate goal is to understand the toxic radiation that devastated his people and concoct a cure for the afflicted leper gnomes.",h="Following earlier inconclusive tests on surface troggs, Ozzie Togglevolt tasks adventurers with retrieving...",sec={{t="A Pure Sample",b="Ozzie Togglevolt's preliminary trials outside the city were a failure. The irradiated troggs roaming Dun Morogh carried insufficient and impure residue, leaving his lab in Kharanos with more questions than answers. To engineer a true remedy for leper gnomes, Togglevolt concludes that scientific integrity demands a fresh, concentrated sample directly from deep within the city's toxic belly.",sp=0},{t="Straight from the Tap",b="Obtaining fallout of sufficient potency means braving Gnomeregan itself. The lower depths around the Hall of Gears and Clean Zone teem with irradiated horrors, lurkers, and slimes spawned by the disastrous venting of radioactive waste. Extracting this unstable ooze into a heavy leaden phial is hazardous work: the fallout rapidly degrades, making containment extremely volatile and time-sensitive.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why does Ozzie need radioactive fallout?",a="Ozzie Togglevolt is trying to synthesize a cure for the leper gnomes, whose minds and bodies were ruined by the fallout released during the fall of Gnomeregan. He believes understanding the undiluted poison is the first step toward reversing its dreadful effects.",al={"ozzie togglevolt cure","why get green glow","cure for leper gnomes"}},{q="Where does the player find the fallout?",a="The fallout must be gathered from living irradiated horrors, lurkers, and slimes found inside the depths of Gnomeregan, particularly in the lower levels around the Hall of Gears and past the Clean Zone.",al={"where is high potency radioactive fallout","fallout location gnomeregan"}},{q="Why were the surface trogg samples rejected?",a="The troggs wandering outside Gnomeregan did not carry enough concentrated contamination. Their samples were too weak and impure to serve as reliable research material for Ozzie's cure experiments.",al={"why not troggs","what was wrong with gnogaine"}},{q="Why is the fallout on a time limit?",a="The fallout is highly unstable and active. Even inside a leaden collection phial, the volatile radiation breaks down rapidly, forcing researchers to return it to the laboratory in Kharanos before it loses its potency.",al={"why does fallout expire","fallout duration"}},{q="Who are the leper gnomes Ozzie hopes to help?",a="Leper gnomes are former citizens of Gnomeregan who were trapped inside when the radiation valves opened to combat the troggs. Instead of dying, they mutated into sickened, deranged survivors hostile to their former kin.",al={"leper gnomes lore","what are leper gnomes"}},{q="Who assigns this task?",a="The quest is assigned by Ozzie Togglevolt, a gnome researcher stationed out of Kharanos in Dun Morogh who is dedicated to remedying the aftermath of Gnomeregan's catastrophe.",al={"who gives the quest","ozzie togglevolt location"}}},ang={["race:Gnome"]="Every gnome carries the grief of their lost home. Helping Ozzie test whether the horrific mutation can be undone strikes at the heart of their hopes to redeem their fallen kin.",["profession:Engineering"]="The volatile nature of radiation containment requires sturdy lead shielding and precise instruments, illustrating the catastrophic consequences when engineering fails.",["faction:Alliance"]="Stabilizing Dun Morogh and reclaiming Gnomeregan requires understanding the lethal hazards still corrupting Ironforge's doorstep."},kw={"gnogaine","gnomeregan","hall of gears","kharanos","leper gnome","ozzie togglevolt","radiation","radioactive fallout"},rel={"quest:2926","quest:2927","npc:ozzie-togglevolt","zone:gnomeregan","topic:leper-gnome","subzone:hall-of-gears","subzone:clean-zone","subzone:kharanos"},m={start="Ozzie Togglevolt",level="30",faction="Alliance",id=2962},src={"The Only Cure is More Green Glow"}}
E["subzone:clean-zone"] = {t="subzone",n="Clean Zone",z="gnomeregan",s="The Clean Zone is a fortified, decontamination enclave nestled inside the ruined city of Gnomeregan just past the upper Hall of Gears. It serves as the sole safe haven within the irradiated facility where uncorrupted gnomish forces hold ground against surrounding troggs and leper gnomes. Here, field medics, technicians, and specialized Sparklematic machines offer respite and salvage operations amid the radioactive ruins.",h="The Clean Zone is a fortified, decontamination enclave nestled inside the ruined city of Gnomeregan just past...",sec={{t="A Bastion in the Slag",b="While most of Gnomeregan succumbed to Mekkatorque's disastrous venting of radioactive waste, the Clean Zone remains untainted. Positioned strategically between the trogg-infested Dormitory below and the contested corridors of the Hall of Gears above, it acts as a fortified forward base. Resolute gnome defenders, technicians, and field medics hold the barricades day and night, ensuring Alliance expeditions have a stable staging ground to regroup, mend wounds, and maintain machinery.",sp=0},{t="The Sparklematic 5200",b="Beyond serving as a military redoubt, the Clean Zone is a hub for salvaging the lost capital. Gnomish engineers installed Sparklematic 5200 units to chemically scrub and wash grime-encrusted relics hauled out of the city's radioactive underbelly. Technicians and merchants like Tink Sprocketwhistle process these reclaimed gears and baubles, outfitting adventurers while studying the lingering toxic fallout that plagues the deep tunnels.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why isn't this area irradiated like the rest of Gnomeregan?",a="The Clean Zone was heavily sealed and actively filtered by gnomish engineering, sparing it from the initial radiation discharge that poisoned the rest of the city. Technicians and active scrubbers work constantly to prevent radioactive contaminants from seeping in from the adjoining hallways.",al={"why clean zone not irradiated","why safe here","clean zone radiation"}},{q="What do the Sparklematic 5200 machines do?",a="Sparklematic 5200s are specialized gnomish laundering and decontamination devices. Adventurers can feed grime-encrusted objects retrieved from troggs and lepers into them, washing away radioactive grime to reveal useful ores, gems, coins, or engineering oddities.",al={"sparklematic 5200","what are sparklematics","clean grime"}},{q="Who controls and defends the Clean Zone?",a="A dedicated detachment of uncorrupted gnomish guards, field medics, and technicians hold the perimeter. They fight off encroaching trogg incursions from the Dormitory and leper gnomes descending from the upper levels to keep the staging post secure.",al={"who is in clean zone","clean zone guards","who holds clean zone"}},{q="Can players safely rest or repair here?",a="Yes. The Clean Zone acts as an operational field camp deep inside Gnomeregan, providing engineering supplies, repairs from vendor Tink Sprocketwhistle, and even a functioning mailbox for adventurers operating behind the front lines.",al={"repairs clean zone","can you rest in clean zone","mailbox in gnomeregan"}}},ang={["race:Gnome"]="For gnomes, standing in the Clean Zone is both a grim reminder of their home's fall and a stubborn beacon of hope that Gnomeregan's technology can still be reclaimed from the troggs.",["profession:Engineering"]="The operational Sparklematic 5200 units and the presence of merchant Tink Sprocketwhistle make this outpost a vital spot for scouring irradiated junk for rare schematics and mechanical parts."},kw={"clean zone","dormitory","gnomeregan","hall of gears","radiation","sparklematic 5200","tink sprocketwhistle","troggs"},rel={"zone:gnomeregan","subzone:hall-of-gears","subzone:dormitory","topic:gnome","topic:trogg"},src={"Clean Zone"}}
E["subzone:clockwerk-run"] = {t="subzone",n="Clockwerk Run",z="gnomeregan",s="The Clockwerk Run is the main entrance corridor leading into the heart of fallen Gnomeregan. Stretching between the Train Depot and the Hall of Gears, this damaged hallway is heavily contaminated by toxic fallout and overrun with irradiated troggs.",h="The Clockwerk Run is the main entrance corridor leading into the heart of fallen Gnomeregan.",sec={{t="A Ruined Threshold",b="Serving as the primary gateway into Gnomeregan from the outer train depot, the Clockwerk Run was once a bustling conduit of gnomish logistics and transit. When High Tinker Mekkatorque ordered the venting of radioactive waste to stem the trogg invasion, the corridor became a lethal trap. The blast and subsequent fighting caused portions of the hallway to collapse onto itself. Today, the passage is choked with toxic fumes and prowling irradiated troggs, making it the perilous frontline that any expedition must fight through to reach the upper Hall of Gears.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where does the Clockwerk Run lead?",a="The Clockwerk Run connects the Train Depot outside the deep vaults directly to the upper levels of the Hall of Gears inside Gnomeregan.",al={"clockwerk run location","where does this hallway go","clockwerk run entrance"}},{q="Why are there so many troggs here?",a="The subterranean troggs swarmed up through Gnomeregan's lower passages during their initial invasion. Those roaming the Clockwerk Run absorbed heavy doses of vented radioactive waste, mutating into violent irradiated troggs that attack anyone attempting to enter the city.",al={"why troggs","clockwerk run enemies"}},{q="Why is the corridor partially caved in?",a="The intense fighting during the fall of Gnomeregan and the catastrophic release of toxic counter-measures caused severe structural damage throughout the perimeter, leaving the corridor partially collapsed onto itself.",al={"clockwerk run collapsed","why is it broken"}}},ang={["race:Gnome"]="Passing through the Clockwerk Run is a bitter reminder of the fall of the capital, showing firsthand how the desperate ploy to cleanse the city mutated the invaders instead of destroying them.",["profession:Engineering"]="The ruined machinery and collapsed infrastructure along the run offer a grim look at what happens when industrial-scale gnomish mechanisms are subjected to catastrophic explosive and radioactive damage."},kw={"clockwerk run","gnomeregan","hall of gears","irradiated troggs","train depot","troggs"},rel={"zone:gnomeregan","subzone:hall-of-gears","subzone:train-depot","topic:trogg","topic:gnome"},src={"Clockwerk Run"}}
E["subzone:dormitory"] = {t="subzone",n="Dormitory",z="gnomeregan",s="The Dormitory is a residential sector within the fallen technological capital of Gnomeregan. Once providing living quarters for countless gnome citizens, it now lies choked with radioactive fallout and crawls with savage, irradiated troggs.",h="The Dormitory is a residential sector within the fallen technological capital of Gnomeregan.",sec={{t="A Home Overrun",b="Situated just past the decontamination chambers of the Clean Zone, the Dormitory formerly housed the inventors, laborers, and families of Gnomeregan. When High Tinker Mekkatorque initiated the emergency radiation venting to combat the invading trogg horde, this densely populated sector became a trap. Today, its communal halls and living units are completely abandoned by gnomish life, occupied instead by mutated troggs that thrive in the radioactive miasma. Travelers descending toward the lower levels of the city must fight through this tragic reminder of the catastrophe to reach the lower Hall of Gears.",sp=0},{t="Punchograph Terminals",b="Amid the clutter of abandoned bunks and mutated subterranean invaders, remnants of the city's intricate administrative apparatus still function. The Matrix Punchograph 3005-B machines reside in this sector, processing the punched security data cards carried by gnome personnel. These automated terminals allow surviving gnomes and their allies to retrieve and encode authorization cards needed to access deeper city sectors and secure archival vaults.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What was the Dormitory used for before the fall?",a="The Dormitory served as everyday living quarters for Gnomeregan's vast population of inventors, workers, and their families. Its proximity to industrial and civic sectors allowed gnome citizens easy access between their workstations and resting bunks before toxic radiation flooded the lower corridors.",al={"what is dormitory","dormitory purpose","who lived here"}},{q="Why is the Dormitory infested with troggs?",a="When the troggs breached the city from beneath, High Tinker Mekkatorque flooded the city with toxic gas to kill them. Instead of wiping them out, the radiation mutated the surviving troggs, making them more vicious and entirely resistant to the irradiated environment of the residential blocks.",al={"why troggs here","trogg infestation dormitory","irradiated troggs"}},{q="Where does the Dormitory lead?",a="The Dormitory sits just beyond the sanitized airlocks of the Clean Zone and connects the upper levels to the lower level of the Hall of Gears, making it an unavoidable chokepoint for anyone pushing deeper into Gnomeregan.",al={"dormitory exits","where to go from dormitory","dormitory connections"}},{q="What are the Matrix Punchograph machines found here?",a="The Matrix Punchograph 3005-B terminals are automated data processing stations. Gnomish security protocols rely on punch cards, and these machines are used to upgrade and encode data cards to bypass security checkpoints deeper inside the facility.",al={"punchograph","matrix punchograph 3005-B","punch cards"}}},ang={["race:Gnome"]="Stepping into the Dormitory is personal for every gnome: this was once your home, now reduced to irradiated rubble and overrun by the very brutes who drove you from it.",["profession:Engineering"]="Even amid total bio-containment failure, automated terminals like the Matrix Punchograph 3005-B continue processing algorithmic security punch cards flawlessly."},kw={"clean zone","dormitory","gnomeregan","hall of gears","punchograph","trogg"},rel={"zone:gnomeregan","subzone:clean-zone","subzone:hall-of-gears","topic:gnome","topic:trogg"},src={"Dormitory"}}
E["subzone:engineering-labs"] = {t="subzone",n="Engineering Labs",z="gnomeregan",s="The Engineering Labs are a multi-tiered research and manufacturing facility deep within Gnomeregan. Connected to the Workshop Entrance and Launch Bay, this bustling center of gnome innovation was overrun during the city's radioactive cataclysm and is now swarming with crazed leper gnomes and rogue mechanical contraptions.",h="The Engineering Labs are a multi-tiered research and manufacturing facility deep within Gnomeregan.",sec={{t="A Fallen Center of Innovation",b="Built around a central mechanical structure, the Engineering Labs span two primary tiers connected by a central cargo lift. In Gnomeregan's prime, tinkerers here developed schematics and fine-tuned clockwork inventions. Today, radiation leaks have driven the remaining researchers mad, transforming them into deranged leper gnomes who mindlessly guard malfunctioning machinery alongside rogue constructs.",sp=0},{t="Crucial Junction",b="Beyond its historical role as a laboratory, the chamber serves as a vital transit hub through the lower reaches of the ruined city. Passages wind toward the Launch Bay, Tinkers' Court, and the Workshop Entrance back door. The lower floor also houses the Matrix Punchograph 3005-D terminals, critical processing units required to decipher the coded punch cards carried by gnome engineers.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What were the Engineering Labs originally used for?",a="Before the city fell, the Engineering Labs were dedicated to research, assembly, and testing of complex gnome contraptions and automated devices. Gnomish engineers and technicians used the vast two-level chamber to blueprint new technology.",al={"purpose of engineering labs","what was made here","engineering labs lore"}},{q="What threats roam the Engineering Labs now?",a="Irradiated leper gnomes and haywire mechanical automatons roam both tiers of the chamber. These lingering residents were driven completely mad by the irradiated gas released during the city's fall and attack any non-irradiated intruders on sight.",al={"who is inside","enemies in engineering labs","monsters here"}},{q="What are the Matrix Punchograph 3005-D machines?",a="These automated gnomish data terminals are found on the lower level of the Engineering Labs. They allow engineers and adventurers to punch encoded data cards, advancing their security clearance and deciphering technical archives preserved within the city.",al={"punchograph d","matrix punchograph 3005-d","yellow card machine"}},{q="How does this area connect to the rest of Gnomeregan?",a="The upper level connects directly to the Workshop Entrance back door and passages leading to the Launch Bay. The lower level leads to the main corridors connecting the Launch Bay and Tinkers' Court.",al={"where does this lead","engineering labs exits","routes to engineering labs"}}},ang={["profession:Engineering"]="The Engineering Labs represent the pinnacle of fallen gnomish automation, retaining functional automated punchograph terminals and discarded schematics amid the wreckage.",["race:Gnome"]="For exiled gnomes, these laboratories are a tragic sight: once the beating heart of their race's technological triumphs, now reduced to an irradiated ruin overrun by their corrupted kin."},kw={"engineering labs","gnomeregan","launch bay","leper gnome","punchograph","tinkers court","workshop entrance"},rel={"zone:gnomeregan","subzone:workshop-entrance","subzone:launch-bay","subzone:tinkers-court","topic:leper-gnome","topic:gnome","npc:umpi"},src={"Engineering Labs"}}
E["subzone:hall-of-gears"] = {t="subzone",n="Hall of Gears",z="gnomeregan",s="The Hall of Gears is a multi-tiered industrial chamber situated inside the fallen city of Gnomeregan, just past the Clockwerk Run. Once a bustling center of mechanical movement, it has fallen into ruin, flooded with toxic sludge, roaming oozes, and irradiated troggs.",h="The Hall of Gears is a multi-tiered industrial chamber situated inside the fallen city of Gnomeregan, just...",sec={{t="A Fractured Machine",b="Positioned just beyond the Clockwerk Run, the Hall of Gears illustrates the catastrophic collapse of the gnome capital. Divided into two main levels, the chamber's upper catwalks are held by aggressive, irradiated troggs that claw through collapsed access shafts. Below, the floor sits drenched in pools of radioactive fallout, where corrosive slimes and living poison elementals thrive in the toxic runoff.",sp=0},{t="Pathways through the Waste",b="The chamber serves as a critical junction deep within Gnomeregan's operational quarters. From its upper walkways, paths branch toward contaminated dead ends and the relative safety of the Clean Zone and the Dormitory. Descending into the radioactive depths below eventually leads travelers through winding maintenance passages toward the Launch Bay, though navigating either floor requires cutting through the lingering horrors of Sicco Thermaplugg's devastating venting scheme.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is the Hall of Gears located?",a="The Hall of Gears lies deep inside the dungeon of Gnomeregan, directly following the Clockwerk Run. It connects further inward toward the Clean Zone, the Dormitory, and the Launch Bay.",al={"hall of gears location","where is hall of gears","how to get to hall of gears"}},{q="Why is the lower level full of radioactive sludge?",a="When High Tinker Mekkatorque ordered the venting of radioactive gas to repel the trogg invasion, the contaminated runoff collected in the city's low-lying machinery halls, turning the lower floor of the Hall of Gears into a toxic wasteland.",al={"why is it green","radioactive waste hall of gears","what is the sludge"}},{q="What creatures inhabit this chamber?",a="The upper level is infested with mutated, irradiated troggs pouring through breach tunnels. The lower tier is filled with radioactive fallout slimes, oozes, and volatile poison elementals that formed from the industrial runoff.",al={"hall of gears enemies","what lives in hall of gears","hall of gears mobs"}},{q="Where do the exits lead from here?",a="The upper walkways lead southwest toward the Clean Zone and the Dormitory, as well as a dead-end maintenance corridor to the southeast. The lower irradiated floor features a winding passage to the west that leads directly into the Launch Bay.",al={"hall of gears exits","where to go from hall of gears"}}},ang={["race:Gnome"]="Seeing the massive cogs and catwalks submerged in irradiated sludge is a painful reminder of the desperate decision that poisoned the city and drove the gnome race into exile.",["profession:Engineering"]="The sheer scale of the automated gearing and elevated platforms displays the pinnacle of pre-fall gnomish engineering, though now heavily corroded by radioactive fallout."},kw={"clean zone","clockwerk run","dormitory","gnomeregan","hall of gears","launch bay","radioactive","troggs"},rel={"zone:gnomeregan","subzone:clockwerk-run","subzone:clean-zone","subzone:dormitory","subzone:launch-bay","npc:sicco-thermaplugg","topic:trogg","topic:gnome"},src={"Hall of Gears"}}
E["subzone:launch-bay"] = {t="subzone",n="Launch Bay",z="gnomeregan",s="The Launch Bay is a subterranean airfield and hangar tucked within the depths of Gnomeregan, located just beyond the Hall of Gears. Once the staging ground for gnomish flying machines and bombers, it has fallen completely under the control of hostile leper gnomes and corrupted mechanical contraptions.",h="The Launch Bay is a subterranean airfield and hangar tucked within the depths of Gnomeregan, located just...",sec={{t="A Grounded Airfield",b="Serving as the primary hangar for Gnomeregan's aerial fleet, the Launch Bay is split across two tiers. Its central platform, reached by ramps from the upper walkway, still houses parked gnomish flying machines and heavy bombers that never made it out before the city was evacuated. Instead of skilled pilots, the flight decks are now crawling with crazed leper gnomes who maintain and guard the idling war machines.",sp=0},{t="Crossroads of the Deep City",b="Beyond its military role, the Launch Bay serves as a vital junction within the complex. Ramps from its southeastern corridor descend into the Engineering Labs, while a southern passage on the lower deck is choked with invading Dark Iron dwarves. That southern tunnel provides a perilous path toward the heart of the city at Tinkers' Court.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Launch Bay used for?",a="It was designed as an underground airfield and maintenance hangar for gnomish flying machines and bombers. Today, it stands neglected and repurposed by the leper gnomes dwelling in the ruins.",al={"gnomeregan hangar","what is launch bay","launch bay purpose"}},{q="Who controls the Launch Bay now?",a="The upper and lower levels are occupied by leper gnomes alongside aggressive mechanical contraptions. Further down near the southern exits, hostile Dark Iron dwarves have also carved out a foothold.",al={"who is in launch bay","launch bay enemies","who lives here"}},{q="Where does the Launch Bay lead?",a="The upper eastern tunnel leads back to the Hall of Gears. The southeastern ramps connect down to the Engineering Labs, while a southern lower tunnel pushes deeper into Gnomeregan toward Tinkers' Court.",al={"launch bay exits","how to leave launch bay","launch bay directions"}},{q="Are the flying machines here operational?",a="Several gnomish flying machines and bombers remain parked on the central platforms, but they sit idle and untended amid the chaos of the city's fall.",al={"can i fly the planes","flying machines gnomeregan","hangar planes"}}},ang={["race:Gnome"]="Seeing the crown jewels of gnomish aviation—flying machines and bombers—abandoned and crawled over by irradiated leper kin is a bitter reminder of the city's tragic loss.",["profession:Engineering"]="The hangar showcases peak gnomish aeronautics and vehicle chassis, though scavengers must contend with hostile contraptions to get a close look."},kw={"bomber","dark iron","engineering labs","flying machine","gnomeregan","hangar","launch bay","leper gnome"},rel={"zone:gnomeregan","subzone:hall-of-gears","subzone:engineering-labs","subzone:tinkers-court","topic:leper-gnome","topic:gnome"},src={"Launch Bay"}}
E["subzone:loading-room"] = {t="subzone",n="Loading Room",z="gnomeregan",s="The Loading Room is an industrial staging chamber inside Gnomeregan's sprawling mechanical complex. In the current era, this subterranean staging area lies deep within the corrupted fallen capital, dangerously close to rogue constructs such as Techbot.",h="The Loading Room is an industrial staging chamber inside Gnomeregan's sprawling mechanical complex.",sec={{t="Industrial Depot Under Siege",b="Before the fall of Gnomeregan, the Loading Room functioned as a bustling transit point and cargo staging bay linked to the subterranean transit networks of the tinker capital. Today, like the rest of the ruined city, it has succumbed to chaos. Radioactive fallout, invading troggs, and malfunctioning machinery have rendered the area extremely perilous. The rogue mechanized construct Techbot guards the vicinity, posing a severe threat to any gnome survivors or daring Alliance reclaimers attempting to secure the perimeter.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Loading Room used for?",a="Historically, it served as an industrial loading bay and cargo staging point connected to Gnomeregan's internal transport and train facilities. Since the city's fall, it has become another lost sector overrun by hazards.",al={"loading room purpose","what is loading room","what was loading room"}},{q="What threats can be found in the Loading Room?",a="The Loading Room is home to the haywire mechanical defense construct known as Techbot, along with surrounding radioactive contamination and erratic machinery lingering in the depths of the city.",al={"who is in loading room","loading room bosses","techbot location"}},{q="Is the Loading Room safe to explore?",a="No. The entire district is contested ground inside the ruins of Gnomeregan. Any Alliance strike team venturing into this part of the complex must contend with hostile constructs and toxic conditions.",al={"is it safe","can alliance go here"}}},ang={["race:Gnome"]="For gnomish reclaimers, the Loading Room is a bitter reminder of how everyday city infrastructure was violently abandoned during the trogg invasion and toxic catastrophe.",["profession:Engineering"]="The rogue construct Techbot and the mechanical assemblies remaining in the Loading Room offer engineers a stark lesson in what happens when automated defenses malfunction without maintenance."},kw={"dun morogh","gnomeregan","loading room","techbot","tinkertown","train depot"},rel={"zone:gnomeregan","subzone:train-depot","subzone:dormitory","topic:gnome"},src={"Loading Room"}}
E["subzone:tinkers-court"] = {t="subzone",n="Tinkers' Court",z="gnomeregan",s="Tinkers' Court is the grand council chamber at the heart of Gnomeregan. Once the bustling seat of the High Tinker and his ruling council, it is now the grim stronghold of the traitor Mekgineer Thermaplugg.",h="Tinkers' Court is the grand council chamber at the heart of Gnomeregan.",sec={{t="Seat of the Gnomish Council",b="Before the disaster that ruined Gnomeregan, the Tinkers' Court served as the civic and political heart of the nation. It was here that High Tinker Gelbin Mekkatorque gathered with advisors and master inventors, including Tinkmaster Overspark, to debate technological advancements, govern civic matters, and guide gnomish society. The court represented the pinnacle of gnomish ingenuity and governance, situated just beyond the industrial works of the Engineering Labs and the Launch Bay.",sp=0},{t="Thermaplugg's Throneroom",b="Following the disastrous radiation venting that drove the gnomes into exile, Mekgineer Sicco Thermaplugg claimed the chamber as his own. Styling himself the King of Gnomeregan, the mad inventor now sits in the Tinkers' Court surrounded by twisted contraptions, loyal leper gnomes, and bomb dispensers. From this desecrated council hall, he directs his remaining forces, making the court the final and most dangerous threshold for any strike team seeking to end his rule.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What was the Tinkers' Court used for originally?",a="Historically, the Tinkers' Court served as the meeting place and civic chamber for the elected High Tinker and the ruling council of Gnomeregan. Gelbin Mekkatorque and high-ranking advisors, such as Tinkmaster Overspark, used this hall to discuss city governance and cutting-edge innovations.",al={"tinkers court history","what is tinkers court","original purpose of court"}},{q="Who controls Tinkers' Court now?",a="Mekgineer Sicco Thermaplugg currently occupies the court. Calling himself the King of Gnomeregan, he holds the chamber alongside his defensive machinery and irradiated minions.",al={"who is in tinkers court","boss in tinkers court","thermaplugg room"}},{q="Where is the court located within Gnomeregan?",a="Tinkers' Court lies in the deepest reaches of Gnomeregan, beyond the dark tunnels and lower levels connected to both the Launch Bay and the Engineering Labs.",al={"where is tinkers court","how to get to tinkers court","find tinkers court"}},{q="Why is reaching Tinkers' Court so important for the Alliance?",a="Reaching the court is the ultimate objective of reclaiming the city, as Mekgineer Thermaplugg directs his irradiated minions from within. Deposing him is the critical first step toward Gnomeregan's liberation.",al={"why go to tinkers court","kill thermaplugg why","importance of tinkers court"}}},ang={["race:Gnome"]="Standing in the Tinkers' Court is a painful reminder of betrayal; this room was once where gnomish leaders gathered before Sicco Thermaplugg seized it amidst irradiated ruin.",["profession:Engineering"]="The chamber is an alarming showcase of corrupted engineering, filled with deadly bomb delivery systems and the lethal siege suit operated by Thermaplugg."},kw={"council","gnomeregan","high tinker","mekkatorque","overspark","thermaplugg","tinkers court"},rel={"zone:gnomeregan","npc:gelbin-mekkatorque","quest:2923","subzone:engineering-labs","subzone:launch-bay","topic:gnome"},src={"Tinkers' Court"}}
E["subzone:train-depot"] = {t="subzone",n="Train Depot",z="gnomeregan",s="The Train Depot is a subterranean transit hub located just below the surface entrances of Gnomeregan in Dun Morogh. Once a bustling center of gnomish locomotion, it now swarms with hostile leper gnomes and invading troggs.",h="The Train Depot is a subterranean transit hub located just below the surface entrances of Gnomeregan in Dun...",sec={{t="A Ruined Transit Hub",b="Situated at the bottom of the grand elevator leading down from Dun Morogh, the Train Depot once served as the primary nexus for rail transport across the subterranean marvel of Gnomeregan. Today, the platforms and railbeds lie in shambles. The fallout that irradiated the city transformed its remaining workers into crazed leper gnomes, while subterranean troggs have overrun the tracks. Explorers descending into the ruined city must navigate this staging ground to reach deeper sectors such as Clockwerk Run, the Loading Room, and the inner engineering facilities.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is the Train Depot located?",a="The Train Depot lies directly beneath the surface entrance elevator in Dun Morogh, acting as one of the outer threshold areas before venturing into the core of Gnomeregan.",al={"train depot location","how to get to train depot","train depot entrance"}},{q="What creatures inhabit the Train Depot now?",a="The depot is overrun by feral troggs who burrowed up from the deep earth and wretched leper gnomes who lost their sanity during the radioactive disaster.",al={"train depot enemies","mobs in train depot","who is in train depot"}},{q="Where do the paths from the Train Depot lead?",a="Passages lead west into Clockwerk Run and toward the Loading Room, while a northern workshop area houses a back door down into the upper Engineering Labs.",al={"train depot exits","where does train depot go","train depot connections"}},{q="Who is hiding in the Train Depot?",a="Namdo Bizzfizzle, an engineering supplier, manages to survive tucked away beneath the north side of the main platform on the depot's lower level.",al={"namdo bizzfizzle","train depot npc","train depot vendor"}}},ang={["race:Gnome"]="For exiled gnomes, the abandoned depot is a tragic sight, showing the ruin of the advanced locomotion systems that once united their subterranean metropolis.",["profession:Engineering"]="Engineers seeking rare schematics often scout the depot's lower platforms, where surviving gnome peddlers like Namdo Bizzfizzle still ply their trade amidst the wreckage."},kw={"clockwerk run","dun morogh","gnomeregan","leper gnome","loading room","namdo bizzfizzle","train depot","trogg"},rel={"zone:gnomeregan","zone:dunmorogh","subzone:clockwerk-run","subzone:loading-room","subzone:engineering-labs","topic:leper-gnome","topic:trogg","topic:gnome"},src={"Train Depot"}}
E["subzone:workshop-entrance"] = {t="subzone",n="Workshop Entrance",z="gnomeregan",s="The Workshop Entrance, commonly known as the backdoor to Gnomeregan, is an access portal situated just beyond the Train Depot. It provides seasoned adventurers and engineers an alternative route into the depths of the irradiated city, bypassing the front gates and opening near the Engineering Labs.",h="The Workshop Entrance, commonly known as the backdoor to Gnomeregan, is an access portal situated just beyond...",sec={{t="The Backdoor to the City",b="Located across the cavernous workshop floor just past the Train Depot, the Workshop Entrance offers a direct approach into the industrial heart of Gnomeregan. Flanked on one side by the opening to the Loading Room, this passage cuts straight through to the Engineering Labs, avoiding the fortified entry gates that leper gnomes and troggs contest near the surface. For strike teams attempting to reclaim the underground capital, bypassing the initial perimeter through this side door can prove vital.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is the Workshop Entrance located?",a="The Workshop Entrance sits on the far side of the workshop floor, past the Train Depot in the outer corridors of Gnomeregan. From this vantage, the portal to the Loading Room lies to your left.",al={"workshop entrance location","where is the backdoor","gnomeregan backdoor loc"}},{q="Why is this area called the backdoor?",a="It serves as an alternate access threshold into the interior dungeon of Gnomeregan, skipping the main front gauntlet and placing intruders directly toward the Engineering Labs.",al={"why backdoor","gnomeregan back door","back entrance"}},{q="Where does this doorway lead inside the city?",a="Stepping through this portal leads down a hallway directly into the Engineering Labs sector deep inside Gnomeregan.",al={"where does it go","path through backdoor","what is past the entrance"}}},ang={["race:Gnome"]="Every secret doorway into Gnomeregan is a potential breach point for reclaiming lost workshops and recovering prototype machinery from Mekgineer Thermaplugg's forces.",["profession:Engineering"]="This corridor leads directly toward the Engineering Labs, making it an enticing infiltration route for tinkerers seeking cutting-edge schematics."},kw={"backdoor","engineering labs","gnomeregan","loading room","train depot","workshop entrance"},rel={"zone:gnomeregan","subzone:train-depot","subzone:loading-room","subzone:engineering-labs","topic:gnome"},src={"Workshop Entrance"}}
E["zone:gnomeregan"] = {t="dungeon",n="Gnomeregan",z="gnomeregan",s="Carved into the snowy foothills of Dun Morogh, Gnomeregan was once the subterranean capital and greatest technological wonder of the gnomish race. Today it lies ruined and quarantined, poisoned by radioactive fallout following a desperate defense against an underground trogg invasion. Its surviving people now dwell as refugees in nearby Ironforge, while the irradiated halls remain overrun by mutated troggs, deranged leper gnomes, and rogue mechanical sentries.",h="Carved into the snowy foothills of Dun Morogh, Gnomeregan was once the subterranean capital and greatest...",sec={{t="A Marvel of Iron and Steam",b="Long before its tragic fall, Gnomeregan stood as a testament to the heights of gnomish brilliance, ambition, and industry. Constructed with the assistance of the nearby dwarves of Ironforge, the sprawling mechanical complex was powered by giant grinding engines, whirring gears, and an intricate ventilation network that required fifteen technicians working around the clock just to maintain fresh air. It was a thriving center of invention, competitive craft, and politics centered on Tinkers' Court, serving as the proud capital from which gnomes contributed invaluable siege engines, flying machines, and armaments to the Alliance of Lordaeron during the Second War.",sp=0},{t="The Trogg Invasion and the Poisoning",b="Around the time the Scourge tore through Lordaeron during the Third War, a subterranean nightmare stirred beneath Dun Morogh. Unwitting dwarven excavations at the ancient titan vault of Uldaman awakened hordes of primitive troggs, which burrowed into the lower foundations of Gnomeregan. Reluctant to abandon the Alliance in its hour of need by asking for help, High Tinker Gelbin Mekkatorque and his forces fought an agonizing five-year war of attrition against the invaders. When defenses collapsed, Mekkatorque yielded to the counsel of his chief advisor, Mekgineer Sicco Thermaplugg, and authorized venting the city's radioactive waste tanks into the lower levels to eradicate the troggs. Instead, the toxic gas spread uncontrollable catastrophe, wiping out nearly eighty percent of the gnomish population in days.",sp=0},{t="The Mad Mekgineer's Treason",b="The disaster was no mechanical accident. Sicco Thermaplugg, consumed by jealousy over Mekkatorque's election as High Tinker, intentionally allowed the invasion to escalate and planned the toxic catastrophe, plotting to sweep in, slay the troggs, and seize leadership of the survivors. Instead, the disaster spun beyond his control. The radiation failed to kill the troggs, driving them into a violent frenzy, while Thermaplugg himself was trapped within the contaminated lower tiers. Twisted by radioactive sickness into an insane leper gnome, Thermaplugg crowned himself the techno-overlord of Gnomeregan, commanding mindless leper survivors and erratic machineries from his throne in Tinkers' Court.",sp=1},{t="A Fragile Victory",b="High Tinker Mekkatorque currently coordinates the reclamation of Gnomeregan from Tinkertown in Ironforge, dispatching Alliance adventurers into the toxic depths to break Thermaplugg's rule. Slaying the Mekgineer at the heart of Tinkers' Court dismantles his command over the rogue defenses and leper cohorts, delivering long-sought vengeance for his monumental betrayal. Yet a permanent reconquest remains elusive: the deeper tunnels remain choked with irradiated sludge, mutated beasts, and troggs, leaving Mekkatorque to assemble gyrodrillmatic excavationators and formulate broader military plans to one day reclaim his people's ancestral home.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why is Gnomeregan irradiated?",a="When troggs invaded from beneath the earth, High Tinker Gelbin Mekkatorque attempted to exterminate them by opening the pressure valves on the city's radioactive waste tanks on the advice of Sicco Thermaplugg. The plan was meant to flood only the lower sectors, but the deadly toxic radiation seeped throughout the entire city, slaughtering eighty percent of the gnomish population and mutating the survivors.",al={"what happened to gnomeregan","why is gnomeregan green","radiation in gnomeregan"}},{q="Where did all the troggs come from?",a="The troggs were ancient creatures stirred from deep subterranean slumber by dwarven archaeological excavations at the titan complex of Uldaman. Drawn to the vibrations and heat of Gnomeregan's heavy machinery, they dug extensive tunnel networks directly into the lower levels and engineering quarters of the city.",al={"why are there troggs in gnomeregan","trogg origin","trogg invasion"}},{q="Why didn't the gnomes ask the Alliance for help against the troggs?",a="The trogg invasion occurred at the height of the Third War, while the Kingdom of Lordaeron was falling to the Scourge. Believing the survival of the wider Alliance took precedence, High Tinker Mekkatorque chose not to divert human, dwarven, or elven forces away from the northern battlefronts, attempting to handle the invasion internally with gnomish technology and soldiers alone.",al={"why didn't alliance help gnomeregan","did alliance abandon gnomes"}},{q="What are leper gnomes?",a="Leper gnomes are gnomes who survived the radioactive venting of Gnomeregan but suffered severe physical and mental corruption from prolonged exposure. Their skin has turned a sickly pale green, their bodies are blistered and diseased, and their minds have decayed into raving, homicidal mania under the thrall of Mekgineer Thermaplugg.",al={"why are the gnomes green and crazy","irradiated gnomes","leper gnome lore"}},{q="Who is Sicco Thermaplugg?",a="Sicco Thermaplugg was High Tinker Mekkatorque's closest confidant and chief advisor. Driven mad by jealousy and a lust for power, he intentionally engineered the radioactive purge to ruin Mekkatorque and seize the throne. Irradiated along with the city, he now rules as a deranged leper despot from within Tinkers' Court.",al={"thermaplugg","who is the final boss","mekgineer thermaplugg"}},{q="What changes after Mekgineer Thermaplugg is defeated?",a="Defeating Thermaplugg cuts off the leadership directing the leper gnomes and rogue defenses, securing critical technical data and striking a major blow for gnomish morale. However, it does not immediately cleanse the city. Lethal radiation and thick trogg infestations continue to choke the lower corridors, requiring Mekkatorque to prepare deeper excavations before a full reclamation can occur.",al={"do we retake gnomeregan","what happens when thermaplugg dies","is gnomeregan saved"},sp=1},{q="Why are the Dark Iron dwarves inside Gnomeregan?",a="The hostile Dark Iron clan dispatched emissaries into Gnomeregan, represented by the Dark Iron Ambassador. Ever eager to sabotage both Ironforge and the Alliance, the Dark Irons seek an opportunistic alliance with Thermaplugg, hoping to exploit gnomish technology and weaponized machinery for their own war efforts.",al={"dark iron ambassador","why are dark irons in gnomeregan","dwarves in gnomeregan"}},{q="Where are the surviving gnomes living now?",a="Following the radioactive catastrophe, the surviving untainted gnomes fled through the mountains to Ironforge. Their dwarven cousins granted them sanctuary inside Tinkertown, an engineering enclave within the mountain fortress where Gelbin Mekkatorque governs his exiled people while planning their eventual homecoming.",al={"where are gnomes living","gnome home city","refugees in ironforge"}}},ang={["race:Gnome"]="Gnomeregan is the heart of your people's deepest tragedy and enduring shame; venturing within is a harrowing pilgrimage to avenge eighty percent of your fallen race and dethrone the traitor Thermaplugg.",["race:Dwarf"]="Your kinship with the gnomes traces back to when your ancestors helped lay Gnomeregan's foundations, and your excavations at Uldaman inadvertently unleashed the trogg hordes that caused its ruin.",["faction:Alliance"]="The gnomes stood shoulder-to-shoulder with the Alliance in the Second War, and liberating their lost capital from Thermaplugg is vital to restoring their strength within the faction.",["profession:Engineering"]="The ruined city remains an unmatched graveyard of advanced masterworks, schematics, and experimental contraptions, offering invaluable blueprints amidst the lethal mechanical chaos."},kw={"dun morogh","gnomeregan","grubbis","leper gnome","mekkatorque","radiation","thermaplugg","tinkers court","trogg","viscous fallout"},rel={"npc:gelbin-mekkatorque","npc:sicco-thermaplugg","zone:dunmorogh","zone:ironforge","topic:gnome","topic:trogg","topic:leper-gnome","subzone:tinkers-court"},m={levels="29-38"},src={"Gnomeregan"}}
